{"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/29/indie-app-spotlight-laytr-is-a-one-stop-shop-for-logging-everything-you-want-to-find-later/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\" id=\"h-welcome-to-indie-app-spotlight-this-is-a-weekly-9to5mac-series-where-we-showcase-the-latest-apps-in-the-indie-app-world-if-you-re-a-developer-and-would-like-your-app-featured-get-in-contact\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you lose track of things you’d like to reference later, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">Laytr</a> might be a nice solution for you. All of us save things all over the place, whether that be browser bookmarks, built-in bookmarking features within apps, taking a screenshot to hopefully find later, or just leaving a tab open and hoping we find it again later. <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">Laytr</a> aims to be a nice all-in-one solution for keeping track of your digital bookmarks.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1066292\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h3 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">Laytr</a> offers an incredibly organized UI for keeping tabs on everything. It works with the native iOS share sheet, so when you find something, just hit share and click on Laytr. After that, you can set what to categorize it as, as well as when you want to be reminded again.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Within the app, there are three core tabs. The first one is the Now tab, where it highlights things you need to see imminently. There’s Timeline, which lets you scroll ahead and see things based on the date you set the reminder for, and Library, where you can see everything you’ve ever saved, both in categories or grouped together. Beyond that, you can also search.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One differentiating feature is that there’s no sync, even with iCloud, and no accounts. Everything lives on your device in its own separate bubble, and your data will never live on someone else’s server.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">Laytr</a> is available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/laytr-save-read-later/id6803512999\">free on the App Store</a> for iPhone models running iOS 17 and later. You can use the app for free, but for unlimited access you’ll need a $1.99/month or $14.99/year subscription. There’s also a discount on lifetime, which normally fetches $39.99 but can be had for just $24.99 for early adopters.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Features like searching and exporting will never be limited by the paywall, so even if you decide to unsubscribe later, the app will remain usable.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p><a href=\"https://www.anrdoezrs.net/click-5527864-12834157\"><img class=\"aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066442\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Tello-Banner-4-750-x-150-Mac.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all\" alt=\"\"></a></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Laytr-app.jpeg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/22/indie-app-spotlight-cloudgear-brings-all-cloud-gaming-platforms-into-one-tvos-app/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On the Apple TV, gaming is a little bit of an afterthought for developers. Compared to iPhone, iPad, and even Mac – there aren’t a ton of options. Luckily, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> exists as an all-in-one solution for bringing every major cloud gaming platform into one interface. It’s also available for iPhone and iPad.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1065627\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h2 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> supports every major cloud gaming platform: GeForce Now, Xbox Cloud Streaming, Amazon Luna, and Boosteroid. It streams in up to 5K resolution at up to 120FPS, and also supports HDR, 10-bit color, and Dolby 7.1 Surround Sound.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Beyond those details, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> also offers a few nice-to-have features. It supports controller vibration – and if your controller doesn’t have vibration, it’ll use your iPhone’s Taptic Engine. There’s also a feature to hand games off to your Apple TV from the iPhone or iPad app, in case you don’t want to do all the searching on your TV.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">On iPhone and iPad, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> offers home screen widgets – allowing you to bookmark games and quickly launch into them without interacting with anything else.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-gallery alignwide has-nested-images columns-default is-cropped wp-block-gallery-1 is-layout-flex wp-block-gallery-is-layout-flex\">\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img decoding=\"async\" data-id=\"1065633\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=800\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1065633\" srcset=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg 2752w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=155,116 155w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=655,491 655w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=768,576 768w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=1024,768 1024w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=1536,1152 1536w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=2048,1536 2048w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=350,263 350w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=140,105 140w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=1333,1000 1333w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-2.jpg?resize=150,113 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-id=\"1065634\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=768\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1065634\" srcset=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg 1024w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=97,130 97w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=525,700 525w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=768,1024 768w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=262,350 262w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=140,187 140w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=750,1000 750w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=640,853 640w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Screenshot-3.jpg?resize=150,200 150w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 768px) 100vw, 768px\"></figure>\n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Lastly, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> supports AR glasses plugged into your iPhone – like the <a href=\"https://amzn.to/4zCP7t6\">XREAL glasses</a>, allowing you to play games on a massive display right in front of your face.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">CloudGear</a> is available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/cloudgear-pc-gaming-browser/id6751054342\">free on the App Store</a> for iPhone and iPad running iOS 17.6 and later, as well as Apple TV models running tvOS 18.6 and later. For the full feature set, you can subscribe for $1.99/month, $14.99/year, or $39.99 for a lifetime purchase. A 7-day free trial is available for subscriptions, and you can learn more about the app on <a href=\"https://www.cloudgear.app/\">the website</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/CloudGear-aligned.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/15/indie-app-spotlight-notepad-exe-is-an-ultra-fast-lightweight-code-editor-for-your-mac/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Writing a little bit of code shouldn’t be a hassle. Typically you have to set up a project and go through layers of menus before you can even start to write. <a href=\"https://notepadexe.com\">Notepad.exe</a> flips that script, and believes you should start with a blank file first, and figure out the project later – making it much easier to get your idea on paper.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1064769\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h3 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://notepadexe.com\">Notepad.exe </a>comes with a very native-feeling UI, similar to Xcode – but without all of the bloat. It supports running Swift, Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, and Go, all out of the gate. Just write your code, and hit run. If you want to build something further, you can then turn it into a project.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">It offers a Notes library for easily sifting through all of your files you’ve created, without needing to remember where you created your one-off file.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Notepad.exe also offers a built-in agentic coding assistant, allowing you to use your Codex subscription or local models for troubleshooting problems in your codebase.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And, as a cherry on top – it has a sweet option to bring your simulator inside of the text editor, making it a great workflow for iOS developers writing SwiftUI.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image alignwide size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1064772\" srcset=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png 2880w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=155,97 155w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=655,409 655w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=768,480 768w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=1024,640 1024w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=1536,960 1536w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=2048,1280 2048w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=350,219 350w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=140,88 140w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=1600,1000 1600w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/image.png?resize=150,94 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2880px) 100vw, 2880px\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://notepadexe.com\">Notepad.exe</a> can be downloaded from the developer’s website <a href=\"https://notepadexe.com\">here</a>. For the core experience, the app is free with no account needed. For the fully-featured experience, you can buy Notepad.exe Pro, which’ll run you $19.99/year or $45 for a perpetual license to all updates within version 1.x.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/IMG_0048.jpeg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/534-maxime-heckel":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://maximeheckel.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Maxime Heckel</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> is a software engineer originally from France, now based in New York City. </span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He is currently working as a product engineer at Linear.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">In his spare time, he loves to tinker with frontend development, WebGL/WebGPU, shaders, and graphics programming at large. This area of computer science is an endless source of knowledge and he has spent the past 5 years learning as much as possible.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He’s documenting all of these learnings and distilling them into experiments and essays that he wished existed when he was getting started on his blog which is also his longest ongoing side project (8 years this year).</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What items are in your workspace?</span></h2></p><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Books</span></h2></p><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">(I'm not a huge fan of \"tech books\" despite working in tech, but these are 3 books I really enjoyed and that coincidentally fit my desk aesthetic quite well)</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What software do you find yourself using on a regular basis?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-bulletList _1ao94nj0\"><ul translations=\"[object Object]\" class=\"_1ao94nj1\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://arc.net/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Arc browser</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> (at this point you'd have to take this from my cold dead hands)</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://cursor.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Cursor</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> as my main editor (I still write code by hand)</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://openai.com/codex/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Codex</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> (when I do not feel to write code by hand)</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Apple Notes (this is my source of truth for everything, I store and sort inspiration for upcoming projects and topic ideas for blog posts). I like having these available offline and automatically synced across all devices without having to think about it. I trust Apple with my notes although I did set up some scripts to back them up in markdown on a monthly basis \"just in case\" and also to try out other note taking apps</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://superwhisper.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Superwhisper</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> (when I feel to talk to my computer instead of typing)</span></p></div></li></ul></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is the most recent item that you've added to your workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">It's my </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://modedesigns.com/products/sixtyfive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Mode 65 keyboard</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, which I got back in 2024. I missed the first gen Mode 65 and was pretty sad about it so the moment they released the second version of it, I jumped on it and immediately bought it. It's my first mechanical keyboard. I picked this one for its:</span></p></div><div class=\"dream-post-content-bulletList _1ao94nj0\"><ul translations=\"[object Object]\" class=\"_1ao94nj1\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">material used: it feels heavy and premium, it's all aluminium</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I opted for a Copper accent to add a subtle pop of color to the desk</span></p></div></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is one change you'd like to make to your current workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">My biggest regret is opting for the VESA-mounted Studio Display instead of the one with the adjustable mount. My girlfriend has it, and it feels so much better to adjust than my monitor arm. Since this display now has a second generation version, I may get tempted to upgrade it and finally scratch that itch.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Another small detail concerns my laptop stands, ideally, I'd have them hidden behind my monitor to keep the desk surface clear since it's pretty small. I've seen several people 3D print custom mounts for their MacBooks, but I haven't attempted that yet.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Walk us through your morning routine—what’s the first thing you do at your desk?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">First thing is bringing in my small tray with a nice pour over coffee and a quick breakfast (I know eating at one's desk is not a good habit, but I still do it)</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">While eating and drinking coffee, I catch up on everything work-related: Pull Request reviews from my European coworkers that happened overnight, newly filed issues, etc. I always dread this part because you can quickly get flooded with information first thing in the morning, which is why I pair it with coffee to make it a bit more enjoyable. I try to get it out of the way as soon as possible so I can organize my day quickly</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What’s one productivity trick that actually works for you?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I have many side projects going on, including my blog and shader-related work. It can feel overwhelming, especially when learning about a brand new topic. I always try to chip away at my task list a little bit daily, for at least 1 hour. The daily goal is always very reachable and doesn't necessitate all this time. In general, once I complete it, I get into the flow and continue working through my project, often pushing further than anticipated.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Another trick is to keep my desk neat and clean after work; I rarely let it get out of control. I'm more willing to sit down and work there if it's orderly.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What’s the most underrated app or tool you use every day?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Not underrated at this point but </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://raycast.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Raycast</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> is the app I interact the most with (besides Linear of course). Here are my favorite extensions:</span></p></div><div class=\"dream-post-content-bulletList _1ao94nj0\"><ul translations=\"[object Object]\" class=\"_1ao94nj1\"><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Window Management: I have keybindings to move my windows around very easily and cycle through different sizes, this lets me keep my desktop environment</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Apple Reminders: Basically pilot everything in Apple Reminders from Raycast to set quick reminders, or reminders using natural language</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Download Video X/Twitter: Any work shared that I wish to consult later ends up in my personal offline archive (I just don't trust anyone to keep their account alive anymore, so I archive a lot of designs, URLs, and in this case videos featuring shaders, animations, etc)</span></p></div></li><li class=\"_11av8sw0\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Quick Links: I have quick links to open my editor for each project and to access their custom URLs, all directly from Raycast</span></p></div></li></ul></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Also, a quick shoutout to </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://mymind.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">MyMind</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> which is the second app I use the most. It's perhaps the most thoughtfully built app I've gotten to use </span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/b2c38fec-b6e2-4d6e-a891-318c70d1c677/Maxime_Heckel_2.jpg?t=1782562332","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/08/indie-app-spotlight-pocket-jam-helps-you-learn-and-practice-your-favorite-songs/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you’re an aspiring musician, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">Pocket Jam</a> might be something you find useful. It helps you turn your favorite songs into a practice tool, letting you slow down, change the pitch, loop, and dissect tracks as you learn them.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1063949\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h3 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Of course, if you want to learn to practice a song, you can just listen to it on your phone, pause accordingly, and try to get the hang of it that way – though it may not be super effective. <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">Pocket Jam</a> gives you the capability to pause a song at the moment you want to practice, then slow it down, adjust the pitch, or play it in a loop. You can even bookmark sections you want to spend more time practicing on.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">Pocket Jam</a> works by allowing you to import audio files or a song from Apple Music, though you do lose some features from Apple Music import – like the ability to adjust the pitch.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In the newest 5.0 update,<a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\"> Pocket Jam</a> includes a new redesigned waveform view, making it much easier to navigate through a song, zoom and scrub, jump around, and isolate the parts that matter to you. There’s also a new tempo trainer for starting slow and speeding up as you’re learning, better looping, and bookmark descriptions.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">Pocket Jam</a> is available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/pocket-jam-loop-tempo/id1153284525\">free on the App Store</a> for iPhone, iPad, and Mac running iOS/iPadOS 17 or macOS 14 Sonoma and later. For unlimited imports and music access, you’ll need Pocket Jam Premium, which is $4.99/month with a 3 day free trial, or $29.99/year.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All in all, if you’re someone wanting to learn a new instrument and practice it with some of your favorite songs on your iPhone – Pocket Jam is a great learning tool.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/08/Pocket-Jam.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://9to5mac.com/2026/08/01/indie-app-spotlight-overflight-lets-you-glance-at-what-planes-are-flying-above-you/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"container med post-content\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\n<figure class=\"img-border featured-image\">\n\n\t<img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;w=1600\" class=\"skip-lazy wp-post-image\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?w=320&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?w=640&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 640w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?w=1024&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?w=1500&amp;quality=82&amp;strip=all&amp;ssl=1 1500w\" decoding=\"async\" fetchpriority=\"high\">\n\t</figure>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Welcome to <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/indie-app-spotlight\">Indie App Spotlight</a>. This is a weekly 9to5Mac series where we showcase the latest apps in the indie app world. If you’re a developer and would like your app featured, get <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/author/michaelb\">in contact</a></em>.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If you’re an aviation geek, <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/overflight-sky-radar/id6778497813\">Overflight</a> is a fun new app for iPhone, iPad, and Apple TV that shows you exactly what planes are flying above you, where they’re headed to, and everything else you’d like to know.</p>\n\n\n\n<p><span id=\"more-1062931\"></span>\n\n\n\n</p><h3 id=\"h-highlights\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Highlights</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There are a number of nifty desk gadgets that show overhead flight data, but one thing I find particularly cool about <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/overflight-sky-radar/id6778497813\">Overflight</a> is the fact that it has an Apple TV app – giving you the same always-on nature of a physical product.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image alignwide size-full\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?quality=82&amp;strip=all\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-1062935\" srcset=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg 2048w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=155,78 155w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=655,328 655w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=768,384 768w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=1024,512 1024w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=1536,768 1536w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=350,175 350w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=140,70 140w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=1600,800 1600w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=290,145 290w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=600,300 600w, https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-Apple-TV.jpg?resize=150,75 150w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2048px) 100vw, 2048px\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At a glance, in the free app, you can see the flight number, the tail number, the altitude, speed, nautical mile distance, and more. With pro, you unlock the flight path, can listen to spoken traffic, and see notable inbound alerts – giving you a heads up to look around if something cool is about to pass you. It’ll also never time out if you’re subscribed to pro, whereas free will time out after a short while.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The interface has a neat compass that allows you to point exactly in the direction of the plane as well. I think it’d be neat if there were haptics when you align with the plane you’re trying to spot, but it’s otherwise a cool UI.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When you have a notable inbound alert, the interface will turn amber to highlight its significance.</p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-download-the-app\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Download the app</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/overflight-sky-radar/id6778497813\">Overflight</a> is available for <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/us/app/overflight-sky-radar/id6778497813\">free on the App Store</a> with most of the functionality for all iPhone, iPad, and Apple TV running iOS and tvOS 17 and later. For the full experience, Overflight Pro is available for $3.99/month, $19.99/year, and $69.99 lifetime. A 7 day free trial is available on the subscription tiers.</p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\">\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>My favorite Apple accessory recommendations:</strong></p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Follow Michael: <a href=\"https://x.com/mbrkhrdt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">X/Twitter</a>, <a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bluesky</a>, <a href=\"https://instagram.com/michaelb.nyc\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a></em></p>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"ad-disclaimer-container\"><p class=\"disclaimer-affiliate\"><em>FTC: We use income earning auto affiliate links.</em> <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/about/#affiliate\">More.</a></p></div>\t\t\t\t</div>\n\n\t\t\t\t</div></body></html>","i":"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Overflight-iPhone.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&resize=1200,628","t":"2026-09-05","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/533-tiancheng-luo":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Tiancheng Luo (aka bbbigdear) is a product designer and tech and lifestyle creator focused on workspace aesthetics, modern living, and thoughtfully designed technology. Through cinematic storytelling and hands-on product exploration, he shares tools and objects that blend functionality with visual design.</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What are some of the main items in your workspace?</span></h2></p><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is the most recent item that you've added to your workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">The most recent addition to my workspace is an </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://workspacesxyz.link/LShaped\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">L-shaped standing desk from Vernal</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">. It completely changed the atmosphere of my setup, giving me more space to separate different types of work while making the whole environment feel more organized.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is one change you'd like to make to your current workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I’d love for my workspace to feel calmer and more intentional. Not just on the desk surface, but in a more three-dimensional way. Right now, I feel like the wall space still needs more thoughtful design so the entire environment feels more cohesive and organized.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Walk us through your morning routine—what’s the first thing you do at your desk?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Turning on the speakers. That’s always the first thing I do. Music helps me naturally shift into work mode. After that, I usually check messages, organize ideas for the day, and slowly ease into filming or scripting.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What’s one productivity trick that actually works for you?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I think everyone should eventually build their own unique workflow instead of trying to copy someone else’s. Right now, AI probably makes up around 30% of my studio workflow, so learning how to work with AI tools has become really important for me.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What’s the most underrated app or tool you use every day?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">ChatGPT. I think everyone’s ChatGPT becomes different over time. After months of conversations, it starts understanding you on a much deeper level. For me, it’s not just a tool anymore, but something that helps organize ideas, refine concepts, and challenge my thinking.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/6c438768-b421-4d9b-87d8-065b787f5105/DSC00691.jpg?t=1781356255","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/culture/dogs-working-security-london-waterloo-train-station/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>This article was originally written by Isobel Williams</em> <em>for SWNS — the U.K.’s largest independent news agency, providing globally relevant original, verified, and engaging content to the world’s leading media outlets.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">London’s Waterloo station has become the first major train station in Britain to put dogs on regular security patrols, employing canine colleagues Riley, Buster, and Flo as part of a three-month trial to offer passengers increased safety assurance. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Like a real-world version of the animated kids’ show <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=k9CTlUHNg_Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><em>Paw Patrol</em></a>, the pups were deployed by South Western Railway and Network Rail Wessex in partnership with canine security company Alpha Canine Specialists. And although we know they have very serious jobs, it’s hard not to break out in a grin when looking at their happy faces. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Riley, aged 11, and Buster, aged 9, are cocker spaniels, while Flo, aged 10, is a Labrador. This will be the trio’s final deployment before retirement. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-890x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78646\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-890x1024.jpg 890w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-261x300.jpg 261w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-768x884.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-1335x1536.jpg 1335w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593926-1780x2048.jpg 1780w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 890px) 100vw, 890px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">SWR / NR Wessex / SWNS</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Intended to act as a visual deterrent for wrongdoers, the dogs are part of a wider program designed to keep railway customers and colleagues safe. Other recent measures include equipping staff with body-worn cameras, launching a CCTV upgrade, and investing in a dedicated outreach worker who engages with vulnerable young people around the station. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Security needs constant innovation and we’re taking positive steps to reassure our customers that we take their safety very seriously,” Dan Harrison, station manager at Waterloo, said in a South Western Rails <a href=\"https://www.southwesternrailway.com/other/news-and-media/news/2026/august/paws-on-patrol\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">news release</a>.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He emphasized that the decision to add Riley, Buster, and Flo to the employee roster was a preventative measure. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram wp-block-embed-instagram\">\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DcgsxzaF8qP/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\"></blockquote></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Deploying these dogs is not linked to any increased threat. It’s simply part of providing more visual deterrence and offering our customers some additional reassurance,” Harrison said. “In the same way, we recently equipped all our colleagues with new hi-vis tabards to make them more easily identifiable to customers in the station who might need their help.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While the new job duties might not be <em>quite</em> as thrilling as chasing birds off an airport runway like <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/environment/dogs-chase-birds-keep-airplanes-safe/\">these two border collies do in West Virginia</a>, getting adoring looks from passersby all day comes with its own benefits package.   </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">RELATED: <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/science/how-dogs-process-human-facial-expressions-smiles/\">What’s Going on Inside Your Dog’s Brain When You Smile at Them? Study Reveals How Pups Process Human Happiness</a></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/on-paw-trol-dog-1593927.jpg","t":"2026-09-08","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/humanity/teen-hugh-saetia-eternal-canvas-paints-portraits-grieving-families/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">When Los Angeles-based high schooler Hugh Saetia was 6 years old, he experienced a loss most people don’t grapple with until they’re much older. His mother died. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Following her passing from gastrointestinal cancer, Saetia’s father hired a nanny named Marilyn McAllister to help care for his two sons, and the woman became a strong maternal presence in the boys’ lives. Tragically, around seven years later, in 2024, one of McAllister’s own sons was killed after his shift as a security guard in 2024. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10-814x1024.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78632\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10-814x1024.png 814w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10-239x300.png 239w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10-768x966.png 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-10.png 1168w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 814px) 100vw, 814px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Courtesy of Hugh Saetia</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Saetia as a young child with Marilyn McAllister</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Saetia, then 14, yearned to help the woman who meant so much to him but was unsure how he could best support her. “I always loved art. I always loved paintings,” he told Nice News. “So my dad suggested that I maybe just do a painting of them.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">McAllister, who’d also lost her husband years earlier, followed by her youngest son, was deeply touched by the portrait. “There’s no words to express how I feel about it,” she said. “It’s beautiful. It’s beautiful work.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78638\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png 1152w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png 229w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png 783w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-11.png 768w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1152px) 100vw, 1152px\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>The portrait Saetia made for McAllister of her son Eddie, who died in 2024, with her granddaughter</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Her reaction made a deep impression on her teenage charge, inspiring him to launch his nonprofit, <a href=\"https://eternalcanvas.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">The Eternal Canvas Foundation</a>, which gifts oil paintings of late loved ones to grieving family members. “That moment became kinda like my mission,” said Saetia, now 17. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He began by respectfully approaching mourners at the cemetery where his mom is buried, asking if they’d be interested in a free portrait of their loved one. He paid for supplies — paints, brushes, canvases — with the money he made helping out his dad and brother sharpen knives at a farmers’ market on weekends. Eventually, he started using an internet platform to commission artists across the world, many of whom have experienced loss themselves. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram wp-block-embed-instagram\">\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DZ2wvSMiQ9F/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\"></blockquote></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">About a year ago, he gathered the funds to register the foundation for tax-exempt status under section 501(c)(3), and currently, Eternal Canvas has about 400 active requests. Saetia himself completes as many portraits as he can, a process he admitted can sometimes be emotional. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Grief is something that’s so personal, but it’s universal as well. It’s like everyone experiences it differently, and whenever I’m painting someone else’s lost loved one, I have to remember that this was someone’s life, you know?” he shared. “They had their own world, they had their own story, in a sense. It’s really surreal.” </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram wp-block-embed-instagram\">\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/p/DV6jAAJj22v/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\"></blockquote></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One story that sticks with him involves a portrait he painted of a woman from Samoa. She’d traveled to the U.S. to care for her adult daughter who was battling cancer, but then developed cancer herself. Not wanting to cause her daughter any stress, she kept her diagnosis to herself until her last month. “Her family just commended her for being so strong and keeping that within,” Saetia recounted. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The rising senior, who’s also a school wrestler, said that the portraits reconnected him to art — a pastime he’d enjoyed as a young child but had prioritized less as his interest in sports grew. “I started to fall back in love with art when I started doing Eternal Canvas. So it was a really full-circle moment when I saw what the power of art could do.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">He’s now working on another portrait for McAllister, this time of her husband and sons. “There’s so many other things that he could be doing,” she said, adding, “And you know it’s coming from his heart. He’s putting all of himself into it. It’s just a great thing.”</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large is-resized\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-731x1024.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78600\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-731x1024.jpg 731w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-214x300.jpg 214w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-768x1075.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54-1097x1536.jpg 1097w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/unnamed-54.jpg 1100w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 731px) 100vw, 731px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Screenshot</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>A portrait by Saetia of himself and his late mother, who died when he was 6</em> </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Those interested in requesting a portrait can do so on The Eternal Canvas Foundation website. You can also <a href=\"https://eternalcanvas.org/donate/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">make one-time or recurring donations</a> to help Saetia and his team of artists continue creating paintings.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“I think that I’m giving them almost, like, a doorway into this person’s life,” said Saetia of the people who receive the artwork. “This isn’t just a portrait. It is kind of <em>somebody</em>, you know? Somebody that had a presence on Earth and someone that, for the family, continues to live on in their own hearts.”</p>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/IMG_7367-2-1-1.jpg","t":"2026-09-07","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/science/how-complex-mental-maps-spatial-reasoning-protect-brain/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>This article was written by <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/profiles/hatim-sharif-2426792\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Hatim Sharif</a>, a professor of civil and environmental engineering at The University of Texas at San Antonio, for </em><a href=\"https://theconversation.com/us\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><em>The Conversation</em></a><em> — a nonprofit news organization dedicated to sharing the knowledge of researchers and scientists, under a </em><a href=\"https://theconversation.com/us/who-we-are\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><em>Creative Commons license</em></a><em>. Read the original article <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/taxi-drivers-rarely-die-of-alzheimers-how-complex-mental-maps-and-spatial-reasoning-protect-your-brain-286650\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">here</a>.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Taxi and ambulance drivers are less likely than workers in almost any other job to <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj-2024-082194\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">die of Alzheimer’s disease</a>. That was the surprising result of a 2024 study examining the death certificates of nearly 9 million people in the U.S.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">These findings stopped me in my tracks because those two jobs rely on the same thing as my own work: maps.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I have spent more than two decades staring at maps. Not paper maps on a wall, but digital ones with multiple layers: flood boundaries draped over census blocks, car crash hot spots plotted against road geometry, and satellite readings of rainfall stitched across river basins. Much of my work as a <a href=\"https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=ZJTicOQAAAAJ&amp;hl=en\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">civil and environmental engineer</a> is done through <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/mapping-cemeteries-for-class-how-students-used-phones-and-drones-to-help-a-city-count-its-headstones-273154\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">GIS — that is, geographic information systems</a>. Engineers like me hold several spatial relationships in their minds at once, reasoning about where things sit relative to one another across scales ranging from a city block to a whole watershed.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">I always assumed that spatial reasoning across map layers was purely professional. But that study on taxi and ambulance drivers made me wonder whether all that mental work might be doing something good to the brain.</p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-taxi-driver-brains\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Taxi Driver Brains</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Of the 9 million death certificates from January 2020 to December 2022 that researchers examined, taxi and ambulance drivers had the <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj-2024-082194\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">lowest risk of dying from Alzheimer’s disease</a> out of 443 occupations. After adjusting for age, sex, race, ethnicity, and education, roughly 1 in 100 taxi and ambulance drivers died of Alzheimer’s, compared with 1 in 60 people overall.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This pattern did not extend to other driving jobs. The researchers concluded that the key to reducing the risk of Alzheimer’s was not driving itself but continuous real-time navigation: the constant work of locating yourself in space, tracking a destination, and updating a <a href=\"https://theconversation.com/how-does-your-brain-decide-between-the-road-not-taken-or-the-same-old-route-resolving-conflicting-memories-is-key-to-navigation-279435\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">mental map</a> as conditions change. Drivers whose jobs relied on <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmj-2024-082194\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">fixed or predetermined routes</a>, like bus drivers and aircraft pilots, didn’t seem to experience a similar advantage.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Researchers believe the association between navigation-heavy work and lower Alzheimer’s risk centers on the hippocampus, a part of the brain that governs memory and spatial navigation. It’s one of the first brain regions that Alzheimer’s damages: <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41582-018-0031-x\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Problems with spatial navigation and orientation</a> are among the earliest signs of the disease, sometimes surfacing before obvious memory loss.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In one landmark 2000 study, neuroscientists compared the brains of licensed London taxi drivers with those of people who did not drive cabs. Their findings provided the first evidence via structural imaging that regions of the <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.070039597\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">adult brain can measurably change</a> under sustained navigational demand. To earn a license, London cabbies must memorize more than 25,000 streets within a 6-mile radius of Charing Cross, a challenge known as “<a href=\"https://tfl.gov.uk/info-for/taxis-and-private-hire/licensing/learn-the-knowledge-of-london\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">The Knowledge</a>” that takes three to four years.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Can you memorize 25,000 streets and how to navigate them?</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The researchers found that London taxi drivers had measurably more gray matter in the posterior hippocampus, a brain area tied to storing large-scale spatial maps. That volume <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.070039597\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">tracked with experience</a>: The longer someone had driven, the larger that part of the brain. The change was built through practice, not inherited. While people who are good at navigation might gravitate to this kind of job, the job itself does have an impact on the brain.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Together, these two studies make a coherent case: Work that intensively exercises the hippocampus may reshape it, and that reshaping may protect against one of the most feared diseases of aging.</p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-where-map-specialists-fit-in\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Where Map Specialists Fit in</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Cartographers, urban planners, and geospatial analysts spend their working days in <a href=\"https://www.aag.org/jobs-careers/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">sustained spatial reasoning</a>. A geographic information system specialist might use a computer to overlap population data on flood exposure maps to find who is at risk, or read satellite imagery to map land cover after a wildfire. Researchers juggle several layers of data, coordinate systems and scales at once.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Does spatial reasoning through a screen engage the hippocampus the way moving through a real city does?</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While a taxi driver navigates from inside the scene at street level, GIS researchers picture space from above as a map — what cognitive scientists call <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tics.2006.10.005\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">allocentric reasoning</a>. But these two perspectives overlap in the brain: The hippocampus also builds maps from outside viewpoints, not just from a navigator’s own position.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Research on cognitive maps points toward the same conclusion as the study on taxi drivers. In 2023, researchers ran a machine learning model on more than 22,500 people in a national dataset and were able to predict which ZIP codes had higher rates of Alzheimer’s with 84% accuracy based on how complex the environment was. Those <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.14283/jpad.2023.18\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">living in spatially complex surroundings</a> — the kind that force active map building, such as dense street networks with numerous intersections, diverse points of interest and landmarks, and multiple path options — were less likely to develop Alzheimer’s.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-1024x682.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78556\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-300x200.jpg 300w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-768x512.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-50-1x5k83.jpg 1907w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">fhm—Moment/Getty Images</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Living in spatially complex places challenges your brain.</em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">A follow-up study tied geospatial complexity in one’s environment to greater volume in the brain’s spatial navigation regions. The researchers hypothesized that routinely building cognitive maps <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/dad2.12551\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">exercises the very circuitry</a> that Alzheimer’s attacks first. Repeatedly engaging the cognitive systems involved in spatial navigation could help delay symptoms of disease.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">However, these two studies focus on where people live, not the work people do. Whether spatial reasoning through a screen exercises the same circuitry as real-life city navigation remains untested.</p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-protecting-your-brain\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Protecting Your Brain</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The implications of whether sustained spatial reasoning protects the brain reach beyond mapmakers and cab drivers. Studies have repeatedly found a link between mentally complex occupations and <a href=\"https://www.alz.org/getmedia/ba1ae239-1461-44ec-bc20-d297db776739/ph-bold-center-science-summary-education.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">delayed cognitive decline and lower dementia risk</a>, even after accounting for education.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Research on <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1474-4422(12)70191-6\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">cognitive reserve</a> — the brain’s capacity to continue functioning despite disease — can help explain why two people with a similar disease burden can show markedly different levels of cognitive impairment. If demanding spatial thinking protects the brain, then how societies design schooling, professional training, and retirement all become questions of brain health.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Spatial reasoning <a href=\"https://dx.doi.org/10.1037/a0028446\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">can be trained</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.aag.org/guide-to-geography-programs-and-opportunities/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">training opportunities</a> are already widespread. GIS and remote sensing instruction are available through geography, engineering, public health, and environmental science programs worldwide.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If sustained engagement with spatial reasoning can help the brain strengthen the circuitry that Alzheimer’s attacks first, its value reaches well beyond the technical skills it builds.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">RELATED: <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/health-and-wellness/expert-tips-reduce-alzheimers-risk/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">40% of Alzheimer’s Cases Are Preventable — How You Can Reduce Your Risk, According to an Expert</a></p>\t\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://counter.theconversation.com/content/286650/count.gif\" alt=\"The Conversation\"></figure>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/file-20260805-60-8x6hvk.jpg","t":"2026-09-06","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/environment/what-do-dog-cat-choking-vet/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">At least a few times a month, I Google, ‚ÄúCan dogs eat … ‚Äù followed by whichever of my snacks my Chihuahua mix is eyeing woefully (most recently it was mango, and <a href=\"https://www.purina.com/articles/dog/feeding/can-dogs-eat/mango\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">the answer is yes</a>, in moderation). </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">All loving pet parents want their animal companions to be happy and healthy, and a lot of that comes down to what goes into their mouths ‚Äî so I was taken aback when I realized one day that I had no clue what I‚Äôd do if my pup started choking. Perform the Heimlich? Administer a few slaps to the back? Start running around in circles in complete and utter panic?</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-tiktok wp-block-embed-tiktok\">\n<blockquote class=\"tiktok-embed\" cite=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@20points4gryffindor/video/7637247700546751758\" data-video-id=\"7637247700546751758\" data-embed-from=\"oembed\">  </blockquote> \n</figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To avoid the third option ever becoming reality, I reached out to veterinarian Jinni Sinnott-Stutzman, senior director of clinical affairs for <a href=\"https://vcahospitals.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">VCA Animal Hospitals</a>. She walked me through how to help prevent dogs and cats from choking, as well as what to do if it does happen. Most importantly, though, she reassured me about the rarity of the scenario. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‚ÄúChoking is a scary thing to think about, but I want pet owners to know it’s rare. Pets, like people, are typically protective of their throats,‚Äù Sinnott-Stutzman said, adding that as long as we follow the preventative measures outlined below, ‚Äúit‚Äôs very likely a person owning multiple pets in their lifetime will never encounter choking.‚Äù</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-how-can-we-help-prevent-pets-from-choking\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Can We Help Prevent Pets From Choking?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78584\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-300x200.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-768x512.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1795133707-2048x1365.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Chalabala‚ÄîiStock/Getty Images Plus</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-avoid-choking-size-objects\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Avoid ‚ÄúChoking Size‚Äù Objects</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">One of the most effective ways to prevent your dog or cat from choking is to prevent their access to food and toys that are ‚Äúchoking size.‚Äù Exact measurements will vary based on the breed and individual, but Sinnott-Stutzman explained that choking size is generally the diameter of the <a href=\"https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/body/21869-pharynx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">pharynx</a> (the back of the throat). </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‚ÄúFor a cat or small dog, this is about the size of a plump cherry. For a medium dog, it’s the size of a golf ball, and for your larger dogs, it‚Äôs the size of a tennis ball,‚Äù she said. ‚ÄúSpeaking of tennis balls, that is the most common choke I’ve seen. Typically, large dogs try to catch a ball and miss the timing and get it stuck in the back of their throat. There are <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=V92nhEmKbvs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">great YouTube videos on the exact technique</a> to use to get it out, but it’s a little technical. That said, it can save a life, so I always tell every ER vet to learn it.‚Äù</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Thankfully, tennis balls made specifically for dogs come in various sizes, so if your big pup likes to play fetch, be sure to <a href=\"https://www.chewy.com/kong-squeakair-ball-dog-toy/dp/105550\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">purchase balls on the larger side </a>(rather than standard human tennis balls). </p>\t\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-1024x764.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78578\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-1024x764.jpg 1024w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-300x224.jpg 300w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-768x573.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-1536x1145.jpg 1536w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1372204500-2048x1527.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">nycshooter‚ÄîE+/Getty Images</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For small dogs, it‚Äôs best to opt for the biggest size ball they can actually carry ‚Äî not the teeny-weeny ones, as cute as they may be. </p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-supervise-them\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Supervise Them</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Be sure to never leave your dog unattended with bones, rawhides, balls, and toys that have smaller elements inside (like squeakers), or anything else they can gnaw down or tear apart into choking-size chunks. By supervising them during play, meal, and snack times, you can remove small bits as your pet makes progress on his treat or toy.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sinnott-Stutzman said that cats don‚Äôt often choke ‚Äî but ‚Äúwhen they do, it’s usually on something linear that they are playing with and then start to swallow, so you can usually pull the string, plastic bag handle, or whatever is still sticking out of the mouth to save them.‚Äù  </p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-give-food-in-small-bites\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Give Food in Small Bites</strong></h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">That said, Sinnott-Stutzman has seen very hungry rescue kittens choke on wet food, so be sure to give them small bites for their first meals ‚Äúas they may inhale an entire mouthful and try to swallow it,‚Äù she noted. ‚ÄúOnce they have had a few good meals and are on a positive calorie balance, they can be fed normally.‚Äù</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-1024x701.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78579\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-1024x701.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-300x205.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-768x526.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-1536x1051.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1158693662-2048x1402.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Lisa5201‚ÄîE+/Getty Images</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The same sentiment can be applied to any ravenous dog or cat (and let‚Äôs be honest, even the most well-fed pets often act as though they haven‚Äôt eaten in days). If you give your dog or cat fresh or canned food, ensure it‚Äôs broken up into bite-size pieces. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-how-can-you-tell-if-a-dog-or-cat-is-choking\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>How Can You Tell if a Dog or Cat Is Choking?</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Per Sinnott-Stutzman, there are two kinds of choking. ‚ÄúThere’s discomfort from having something lodged in the back of [the] throat but air is moving through, and there‚Äôs complete obstruction of air movement,‚Äù she explained, noting that the first type ‚Äúis scary to watch, because your pet is gagging, pawing at their mouth, and making really raspy breathing noises. The second kind is scary, period, end of sentence.‚Äù</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The main difference between the two is whether or not the pet is making sounds. If your pet is crying, whimpering, or making rasping sounds while breathing, their airway likely isn’t <em>completely </em>obstructed, but they still need immediate attention. In this instance, you should get them to the nearest open veterinary clinic as soon as possible. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">If they aren‚Äôt making any noise ‚Äî other than maybe a soft gagging sound ‚Äî the airway may indeed be completely obstructed. In that case, jump into action using the instructions below. </p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-steps-to-take-if-your-dog-or-cat-is-choking\" class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Steps to Take if Your Dog or Cat Is Choking</strong></h2>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>1.</strong> Look in your pet‚Äôs mouth and see if there‚Äôs a visible object. If there is, try to grasp it with your fingers and sweep it forward and out ‚Äî but be extremely careful to avoid pushing it further down the airway.<strong> </strong>Sinnott-Stutzman recommends having another person hold open the animal‚Äôs jaws if possible, as even a loving pet may bite when panicked. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>2.</strong> If you can see the object but can‚Äôt get it out with your hands, you can carefully attempt to pull it toward you using the flat side of a spoon with a long handle. Again, be sure not to chase the item further down the throat, and don‚Äôt let go of the spoon once it’s in the animal‚Äôs mouth. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>3.</strong> If you can’t see or remove the object manually, lift your dog or cat up by their back legs, keeping their front legs on the ground to avoid straining the back, and gently shake them. You want to use gravity to move the object out of the mouth. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>4. </strong>If the object doesn‚Äôt come out, try gently swinging your dog or cat back and forth (the key word here is gently) as you hold them from their hind legs. You can also administer five sharp blows to the animal‚Äôs back between their shoulder blades. Use less force for smaller dogs and cats to avoid hurting them. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>5. </strong>If your dog is still choking, <a href=\"https://www.redcross.org/take-a-class/resources/learn-pet-first-aid/dog/choking\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">you can try the Heimlich maneuver</a>. Stand behind or lift the dog with its spine against your chest, then wrap your arms around and under its ribs. Make a fist with one hand, place your other hand over your fist, and give five rapid abdominal thrusts in an inward and upward motion, varying the force based on the size of your pup.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-16-9 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sinnott-Stutzman said she‚Äôs more comfortable recommending the Heimlich for dogs than for cats due to their delicate ribs, but if <a href=\"https://www.redcross.org/take-a-class/resources/learn-pet-first-aid/cat/choking?srsltid=AfmBOop53MrcgkG8ptv-qpukY5aPY_omSHwa4OPvwQUCFv2cqTgbVP7t\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">you do use the technique</a> on felines, use gentler thrusts, and you probably don‚Äôt need to use your entire fist.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>6.</strong> Lastly, if the item is a ball or other round object, Sinnott-Stutzman advocates ‚Äúplaying vet‚Äù by using the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/53kRQTtsWno\">external extraction technique</a>, or XXT.  </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‚ÄúIt’s not for the faint of heart, and again, if your pet is moving air (making noises beyond soft gagging sounds), go to the vet,‚Äù she said. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-video is-provider-youtube wp-block-embed-youtube wp-embed-aspect-9-16 wp-has-aspect-ratio\"></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">‚ÄúBut if they are not, you don’t have a lot of time, so it’s better to try than nothing. Just don’t spend long trying if you’re unsuccessful after one or two tries ‚Äî use the time to get to the vet.‚Äù </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"></p>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/GettyImages-1365277062-scaled.jpg","t":"2026-09-05","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/240-jack-zerby":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://www.jackzerby.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Jack Zerby</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> is currently the Head of Design at </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://gumroad.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Gumroad</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> and Founder of </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://dogma.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Dogma</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://designfordecks.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Design For Decks</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://biddyhq.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Biddy</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"http://getdohq.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">DOHQ</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://Flavors.me\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Flavors.me</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, and </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://www.businessinsider.com/what-is-goodsie-2011-5\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Goodsie</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">. </span><br><br><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He has worked for companies like </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://vimeo.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Vimeo</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://pentagram.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Pentagram</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://frogdesign.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Frog</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://rga.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">R/GA</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> and consulted for companies like </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://teachable.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Teachable</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://americanexpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Amex</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, and </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://staked.us/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Staked</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">.</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What gear is included in your workspace?</span></h2></p><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is your favorite item in your workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">My desk is definitely my fave. It’s got an old classic feel with the benefits of a modern standing desk.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you spark creativity?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Lo-Fi beats station on Spotify and phone on silent. Love sites like siteinspire.com, but will also go to Barnes and Noble and buy a bunch of beautiful magazines in any category.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you manage work-life balance?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I run everything through Notion and create tickets for all tasks for that week along with goals for each quarter. I stop work at 5:30 no matter what, eat dinner and hang with the fam till bedtime. No work on weekends helps clear my mind and prevent burnout.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What do you think is the main benefit of remote work?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">No distractions, no commuting and ability to structure my day around tasks to be completed, not the amount of hours at my desk.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/83ffefc4-12e8-4eba-83aa-2833cea00251/Jack_Zerby_thumbnail.png?t=1781142493","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/c0jzc71f.html":{"c":"<p>智谱昨天活动送2000积分，正好用来判断牛来模型 GLM-5.3-Flash 的耐用程度，看看值不值得买。当然，我们的判断基准线就是opencode go 10刀（大概接近70人民币）来计算。低于这个就不适合买，高于这个就可以买。</p>\n<p>GLM-5.3-Flash 我在使用zcode进行编程开发的时候，我发现Cache 命中率奇低，只有8开头。</p>\n<p>我们先比较纯数值。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"计划\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/5487020260828072600.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>opencode go只给了15刀额度（只代表这个模型只能用15刀，超出部分可以用其他模型）</p>\n<p>那我们就拼一下，15刀的GLM-5.3-Flash+15刀的DeepSeek V4 Flash Vision Exp (Off-Peak)+30刀的DeepSeek V4 Flash (Off-Peak)实现拼60刀。</p>\n<p>按照95%缓存来算，opencode go 大致为24～26 亿 token/月。（不过我目前主力在用 Muse Spark 1.2 Contributor 作为vibecoding首选模型，可以用75～80 亿 token/月）。</p>\n<p>智谱的话lite套餐一个月118元，周10000积分，月40000积分。先当于5小时限额的20倍。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"限额\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/3787420260828075733.jpeg!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>用了大概43分钟跑满了限额（单线程，zcode编程），如果多线程跑会更快。用了大概2千万token。算下来的话目测pro套餐勉强够用。max套餐绰绰有余。</p>\n<p>用量就算出来了，lite套餐 4.3亿token左右。pro 25亿token左右，max 60亿token左右。</p>\n<p>所以说opencode相当于70元买了智谱538一个月的pro套餐了。气笑了。看来国内tokenplan是一个都用不了，国人模型专坑国人诚不欺我。</p>\n<p>目前如果想买到经济实惠的token，tokenplan的主要选择就是 gpt、opencode、commandcode这三种了。</p>\n<p><strong>啥时候能再有一个deepseek涨价之前用opencode的那种实力和价格（相当于之前deepseek v4 flash api 价格除以12）的模型啊。。。</strong></p>\n<p>目前我还在用Muse Spark 1.2 Contributor 勉强度日，还不知道我opencode用完该何去何从了。</p>\n<p>另外：</p>\n<p>用zcode今天可以领3亿token。。。（是时候领鸡蛋了，需要更新到最新版本，点击左下角有个活动卡片，今晚8点开始可用）</p>\n<p><img alt=\"领鸡蛋\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/3822020260828084853.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p><img alt=\"活动说明\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/3094020260828085052.jpg!blogimg\"/></p>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-11","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/mrlh0a7v.html":{"c":"<p>家里跑了好几个服务，Home Assistant、SearXNG、Alist、Emby，还有签到之类的杂七杂八。每个服务一个端口，手机上记端口记到崩溃。</p>\n<p>以前我用 HeoSafe 拦截方案做访问控制，检测到流量直接弹身份认证。能用，但本质上还是请求到了之后再拦，配置维护比较重，算不上好的解决方式。</p>\n<p>后来想通了，干脆把链路整清楚：<strong>ZeroTier 组网 + DNS 域名解析 + iStore Nginx 反代 + certd 证书管理</strong>，一套走通。</p>\n<h2 id=\"硬件和系统\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#硬件和系统\" title=\"硬件和系统\"></a>硬件和系统</h2><p>R5S 软路由刷的 iStoreOS，基于 OpenWrt。Nginx 通过 iStore 应用商店直接装，不是 Docker。这个很重要，因为 iStore 装的 Nginx 有自己一套 UCI 配置，和传统手动装的不一样。</p>\n<p>装完之后 Nginx 自动接管 <code>80/443</code>，uHTTPd 原来的 LuCI 也被接管了，不用额外折腾。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"nginx安装\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/6157220260828054652.jpg!blogimg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"ZeroTier-组网\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#ZeroTier-组网\" title=\"ZeroTier 组网\"></a>ZeroTier 组网</h2><p>ZeroTier 解决的是跨网络访问问题。装完客户端加入同一个网络，设备之间就像在同一个局域网里。</p>\n<p>R5S 上 ZeroTier 分配的内网 IP 是 <code>10.225.17.77</code>。手机、电脑、iPad 加入同一个网络后都能直接访问这个 IP。</p>\n<p>但 IP 记不住，所以需要 DNS。</p>\n<h2 id=\"DNS-解析\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#DNS-解析\" title=\"DNS 解析\"></a>DNS 解析</h2><p>域名 <code>zhheo.com</code> 托管在腾讯云 DNSPod，直接在 DNSPod 加 A 记录：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">s.zhheo.com        → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">heohass.zhheo.com  → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">heodisk.zhheo.com  → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">emby.zhheo.com     → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">qiandao.zhheo.com  → 10.225.17.77</span><br/><span class=\"line\">certd.zhheo.com    → 10.225.17.77</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>这里的 IP 是 ZeroTier 内网 IP，不是公网 IP。所以这些域名只有加入 ZeroTier 网络的设备才能访问，公网打不通。这反而是个安全优势。</p>\n<h2 id=\"Nginx-反向代理\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Nginx-反向代理\" title=\"Nginx 反向代理\"></a>Nginx 反向代理</h2><p>Nginx 装好之后，配一个反代配置文件就行。我放在 <code>/etc/nginx/conf.d/zhheo-services.conf</code>，iStore 的 Nginx 会自动加载这个目录下的 <code>.conf</code> 文件。</p>\n<p>每个域名对应一个后端端口：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">s.zhheo.com        → 127.0.0.1:19080   # SearXNG</span><br/><span class=\"line\">heohass.zhheo.com  → 127.0.0.1:8123    # Home Assistant</span><br/><span class=\"line\">heodisk.zhheo.com  → 127.0.0.1:5244    # Alist</span><br/><span class=\"line\">emby.zhheo.com     → 127.0.0.1:18080   # Emby</span><br/><span class=\"line\">qiandao.zhheo.com  → 127.0.0.1:8923    # 签到</span><br/><span class=\"line\">certd.zhheo.com    → 127.0.0.1:12281   # certd</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>配置模板大概是这样：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight nginx\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/><span class=\"line\">7</span><br/><span class=\"line\">8</span><br/><span class=\"line\">9</span><br/><span class=\"line\">10</span><br/><span class=\"line\">11</span><br/><span class=\"line\">12</span><br/><span class=\"line\">13</span><br/><span class=\"line\">14</span><br/><span class=\"line\">15</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"section\">server</span> {</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"attribute\">listen</span> <span class=\"number\">443</span> ssl;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"attribute\">server_name</span> heohass.zhheo.com;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"attribute\">ssl_certificate</span> /etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.crt;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"attribute\">ssl_certificate_key</span> /etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.key;</span><br/><span class=\"line\"></span><br/><span class=\"line\">    <span class=\"section\">location</span> / {</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_pass</span> http://127.0.0.1:8123;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_set_header</span> Host <span class=\"variable\">$host</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_http_version</span> <span class=\"number\">1</span>.<span class=\"number\">1</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_set_header</span> Upgrade <span class=\"variable\">$http_upgrade</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_set_header</span> Connection <span class=\"string\">\"upgrade\"</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">        <span class=\"attribute\">proxy_read_timeout</span> <span class=\"number\">3600s</span>;</span><br/><span class=\"line\">    }</span><br/><span class=\"line\">}</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>Home Assistant 需要 WebSocket 支持，所以加了 <code>Upgrade</code> 和 <code>Connection</code> 头。其他服务一般不需要，但加上也没坏处。</p>\n<p>改完配置后：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight sh\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">nginx -t -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf &amp;&amp; nginx -s reload -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>iStore 的 Nginx 必须用 <code>-c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</code>，直接 <code>nginx -t</code> 会报找不到文件。</p>\n<h2 id=\"certd-证书管理\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#certd-证书管理\" title=\"certd 证书管理\"></a>certd 证书管理</h2><p>裸 HTTP 能用，但手机浏览器会弹不安全提示。所以用 certd 管理通配符证书。</p>\n<p>certd 也是 Docker 部署在 R5S 上的，自动申请和续期证书。部署方式选的是「主机-部署证书到 SSH 主机」，直接把证书文件写到 R5S 宿主机：</p>\n<p><img alt=\"添加步骤\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/9982320260828054924.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">/etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.crt</span><br/><span class=\"line\">/etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.key</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>部署完成后 Nginx 不会自动读取新证书，必须手动 reload：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight sh\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">nginx -t -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf &amp;&amp; nginx -s reload -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>这里踩了个坑：iStore 的 Nginx UCI 配置里有个选项叫 <code>uci_manage_ssl</code>，默认值是 <code>self-signed</code>。不关掉它，Nginx reload 时会自动生成自签名证书，覆盖掉你刚部署的通配符证书。解决方法：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight sh\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">uci delete nginx._lan.uci_manage_ssl</span><br/><span class=\"line\">uci commit nginx</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>删掉这个选项之后，Nginx 就不会自动搞证书了。</p>\n<p>另外私钥权限设成 <code>600</code>：</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight sh\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\"><span class=\"built_in\">chmod</span> 600 /etc/nginx/conf.d/wildcard.zhheo.com.key</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<h2 id=\"完整链路\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#完整链路\" title=\"完整链路\"></a>完整链路</h2><figure class=\"highlight text\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/><span class=\"line\">7</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">手机/电脑/iPad</span><br/><span class=\"line\">  ↓ ZeroTier 组网</span><br/><span class=\"line\">R5S 软路由（10.225.17.77）</span><br/><span class=\"line\">  ↓ DNS 域名解析</span><br/><span class=\"line\">Nginx 反向代理（80/443）</span><br/><span class=\"line\">  ↓ 按域名分发</span><br/><span class=\"line\">各服务后端端口</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<p>体验上就是：加入 ZeroTier 网络后，手机浏览器直接输入 <code>https://heohass.zhheo.com</code>，无警告、无拦截，直接到 Home Assistant。</p>\n<p>比之前 HeoSafe 的方案清爽多了。</p>\n<h2 id=\"踩坑记录\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#踩坑记录\" title=\"踩坑记录\"></a>踩坑记录</h2><ol>\n<li><strong>iStore Nginx 的 <code>nginx -t</code> 要加 <code>-c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</code></strong>，否则直接报错。</li>\n<li><strong><code>uci_manage_ssl='self-signed'</code> 会覆盖证书文件</strong>，部署正式证书前必须删掉。</li>\n<li><strong>Nginx 不会自动重新读取证书</strong>，部署后必须 reload。</li>\n<li><strong>Home Assistant 的 <code>X-Forwarded-*</code> 头会导致 400</strong>，其他服务的转发头不要随便加到 HA 的 vhost 上。</li>\n<li><strong>DNSPod 刷新有延迟</strong>，刚改完记录可能要等几分钟才能查到。</li>\n<li><strong>Nginx reload 要用 <code>nginx -s reload -c /etc/nginx/uci.conf</code></strong>，用 <code>/etc/init.d/nginx reload</code> 可能触发 iStore 的 SSL 自动生成逻辑。</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"相关地址\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#相关地址\" title=\"相关地址\"></a>相关地址</h2><ul>\n<li>ZeroTier 官网：<a href=\"https://www.zerotier.com/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.zerotier.com</a></li>\n<li>certd 官网：<a href=\"https://certd.docmirror.cn/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://certd.docmirror.cn</a></li>\n<li>DNSPod：<a href=\"https://console.dnspod.cn/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://console.dnspod.cn</a></li>\n<li>iStoreOS：<a href=\"https://www.istoreos.com/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.istoreos.com</a></li>\n<li>OpenWrt Wiki Nginx：<a href=\"https://openwrt.org/docs/guide-user/services/webserver/nginx\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">https://openwrt.org/docs/guide-user/services/webserver/nginx</a></li>\n</ul>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-09","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/252-jack-raines":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He also edits Litquidity's daily finance newsletter, </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://www.execsum.co/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Exec Sum</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He does all of this while being an MBA candidate at Columbia Business School.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Fun facts: He's been deported from Norway, learned how to salsa dance in Argentina, and almost got kicked out of business school for a </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/jackraines/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">satirical LinkedIn post</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">.</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is the gear in your workspace?</span></h2></p><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What is your favorite item in your workspace?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">My Xebec. It's portable and triples my screen size.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you spark creativity?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I've never sparked creativity, it sparks me. Creativity usually hits when I'm in the gym, or on the subway, or at a dive bar at 1 AM. When it does hit, I text myself a few blurbs to review later when I'm by my computer.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you manage work-life balance?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">The best way to manage work-life balance is work on stuff that you don't feel the need to balance.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What does your typical writing process look like?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I sit down, write for 15 minutes, hop on Twitter to look for a tweet that I want to reference, procrastinate on Twitter for 20 minutes, throw my phone on my bed, close Twitter, grind on the newsletter some more.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/2fbcbb73-0bf8-4377-a108-4ac404a2b846/image.png?t=1781141971","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://workspaces.beehiiv.com/p/253-david-heinemeier-hansson":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"_10pdwo80 dream-post-content-doc\"><div class=\"_1gqvddm0\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">He is the creator of </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://rubyonrails.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">Ruby on Rails</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">, the open-source framework that has been used by hundreds of thousands of developers.</span></p></div><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">And if that wasn't enough, he's also a </span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"><a href=\"https://dhh.dk/#driver\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" class=\"_3k8pkd0\">race car driver</a></span><span class=\"hxnnnr0\"> in the FIA World Endurance Championship.</span></p></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What does your typical day look like?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">Early mornings are spent getting kids to school. I usually sit down to work around 8:30. Then it's typically an hour or so catching up on emails, reports, whatever. Then the very best days are entirely free from there to dive into interesting, challenging projects, preferably programming or writing.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">What do you think are the main benefits of remote work in 2023?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I've been working remotely for twenty years, and the benefits remain the same for me. The freedom to live wherever, to work from a home office that provides complete calm for focus, and to enjoy the flexibility of being literally next door to the family during the day. Wouldn't trade it for anything.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"hynlcx0\"><h2 class=\"hynlcx1 hynlcx3\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">How do you personally balance work between multiple ongoing projects?</span></h2></p><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx90\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-blockquoteFigure yuqx93\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><div class=\"dream-post-content-quote _1xtprv91\" translations=\"[object Object]\"><p class=\"_1xtprv92\">❝</p><div class=\"_1xtprv90\"><div class=\"j6zgbu0\"><p class=\"dream-post-content-paragraph j6zgbu1\"><span class=\"hxnnnr0\">I try to work in seasons. Some seasons are dedicated to programming others to writing and others still to working on the business itself. Multitasking is a mirage. All humans can do is thrash. So keeping just one main project on the plate at the time is the key to going quickly.</span></p></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></body></html>","i":"https://media.beehiiv.com/cdn-cgi/image/fit=scale-down,quality=80,width=1200,onerror=redirect/uploads/asset/file/269219fe-657a-455e-9fce-87aaafb183ec/image.png?t=1781141716","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://www.mac52ipod.cn/post/apple-pay-transit-card-support-zhengzhou.php":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"textbox-content\" id=\"zoomtext\"><p>\n\t \tApple Pay 公交支持刷郑州绿城通交通卡了。苹果用户可以在郑州乘坐公交、地铁时直接刷手机或手表，Appley Pay 使用的 NFC 方案只需手机往读卡器上一靠，比扫二维码方便得多。</p><p>其实，Apple Pay 早就通过互联互通卡支持全国几百个城市的公交卡了。但支持本地公交卡有助于用户享受本地公交优惠。比如这次郑州绿城通交通卡给出了公交车 8 折和地铁 9.5 折优惠。</p><p>而且这次新增的也是互联互通卡，到开通一卡通互联的其它 300 多个中国城市也能用。</p><p>iPhone XS、iPhone XS Max、iPhone XR 或更新机型用户，可以将公交卡设为「快捷交通卡」，手机没电自动关机 5 小时内依然可以刷交通卡。所以不用担心「上车后手机没电，没法下车/出站」。注意是自动关机，你长按电源键手动关机就不能刷卡出站了。</p><p>更多开卡方式、城市列表、支持设备等信息，看苹果中国官网关于 Apple Pay 公交卡的详细介绍吧 <u><a href=\"https://www.apple.com.cn/apple-pay/transit/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"苹果中国官网\" rel=\"nofollow\"><font>https://www.apple.com.cn/apple-pay/transit/</font></a></u></p><p><a name=\"entrymore\"></a>\n</p>\n\t<p class=\"textbox-bottom\">\n\t</p>\n\t\n</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/culture/sheboygan-wisconsin-malibu-of-the-midwest-surf/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In the 1970s, Charles Koehler was often one of just two or three surfers in sight as he rode the waves on the shores of Sheboygan, Wisconsin. “I was so naive. I thought, ‘Gosh, the way this is going, I can see where by the time I’m 35, 40 years old [and] I can’t surf anymore, I’m gonna come down here and it’s gonna be 3-foot [waves] and perfect, and there’s gonna be nobody out, nobody to watch.’ Well, that didn’t happen,” Koehler said in the 2025 short film <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1RwUsSblLn4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><em>Dancing With Gravity</em></a>. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Back then, Koehler belonged to a small but enthusiastic cohort who recognized Sheboygan as a hidden gem for surfers. Today, it’s known as the “Malibu of the Midwest” — a hot spot that draws surfers from across the country and beyond each year. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Kingman-Arizona_NatalieStone-1-1024x682.jpg\" alt=\"Malibu of the Midwest sign\" class=\"wp-image-78687\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Kingman-Arizona_NatalieStone-1-1024x682.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Kingman-Arizona_NatalieStone-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Kingman-Arizona_NatalieStone-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Kingman-Arizona_NatalieStone-1-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Kingman-Arizona_NatalieStone-1.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Courtesy of Natalie Stone</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“Malibu was instrumental in shaping the surf scene and culture in Southern California and the world as a whole. Sheboygan was instrumental in shaping surfing on the Great Lakes,” said Andrew Jakus, owner of Sheboygan’s EOS Surf &amp; Rev Board Shop, in an email to Nice News. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Shelly Harms, vice president of marketing and public relations for the nonprofit <a href=\"http://visitsheboygan.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Visit Sheboygan</a>, offered another reason for the comparison, noting that the city’s laid-back spirit, abundance of outdoor recreation, and location on Lake Michigan give it a coastal feel reminiscent of California. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">She also said that twin brothers Lee and Larry Williams helped take Sheboygan’s surf scene to the next level and put the city on the map. “They were surfers who traveled all over and won awards and always talked about their hometown,” she said, adding that the <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dcYgBU4t98E\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">character Chicken Joe in the movie <em>Surf’s Up</em></a> is based on the siblings.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/surf14-Sheboygan-1024x685.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78696\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/surf14-Sheboygan-1024x685.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/surf14-Sheboygan-300x201.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/surf14-Sheboygan-768x513.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/surf14-Sheboygan-1536x1027.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/surf14-Sheboygan.jpg 1774w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Courtesy of Shelly Harms/Visit Sheboygan </figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Harms explained that surfing began to gain popularity in Sheboygan in the 1960s, when locals formed the Lake Shore Surf Club. The sport continued to grow over the years with the Dairyland Surf Classic, founded by the Williams brothers in 1988. “This event brought surfers from all over the world and really brought the focus to Sheboygan as a surf destination,” she said.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em>Step Into Liquid</em>, a 2003 documentary highlighting surf communities around the world, <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2LLk0YhhRdQ\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">featured Sheboygan</a> and solidified its spot on many surfers’ bucket lists, according to Jakus. Although the Dairyland Surf Classic hosted its final competition in 2012 and no comparable surf contest has replaced it, EOS Surf &amp; Rev Board Shop occasionally hosts events, and the local scene continues to thrive. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Aaron-by-Andrew-Jakus-1-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78680\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Aaron-by-Andrew-Jakus-1-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Aaron-by-Andrew-Jakus-1-300x200.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Aaron-by-Andrew-Jakus-1-768x512.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Aaron-by-Andrew-Jakus-1-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Aaron-by-Andrew-Jakus-1-2048x1366.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Courtesy Andrew Jakus</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sheboygan’s position on Lake Michigan is the biggest factor making it a prime surf spot, Jakus said. “With us being central, we can receive waves from both north and south swells. Pair this with our excellent beaches and access, and you have a surfer’s paradise.” Although freshwater waves are generally less powerful than those in the ocean, Sheboygan regularly produces strong, surfable conditions. </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Saltwater surfing also offers more buoyancy, and ocean waves are often easier to catch. Still, many lake surfers welcome the challenge. “In the lakes, everything is like the ocean, but the wave period is shorter, faster, quicker, colder, more erratic, and you’ve gotta be more on your toes if you want to get a good ride,” local surfer Teek Phippen explained in <em>Dancing With Gravity</em>. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-embed is-type-rich is-provider-instagram wp-block-embed-instagram\">\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/Dct0AxwuDYp/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\"></blockquote></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Although surfing is possible in Sheboygan year-round (even in the winter), the scene tends to slow in summer, with peak season occurring in the fall, Jakus told Nice News. “Surfing on the Great Lakes is completely reliant on wind, and in the summer months, you have far fewer weather systems moving around.” </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The city’s best surf spots  depend on the swell direction, but Deland Park, consisting of four different surf spots on the city’s north side, seems to be a consistent favorite. “The Elbow is iconic in Sheboygan surf because you can jump right off the pier and into the lineup,” Jakus said, adding that the Jetties are also a safe bet with easy access. “The whole North Beach/Deland Park area is set up as a perfect little amphitheater to receive swell with grace.” </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Aaron-2-by-Andrew-Jakus-1024x766.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78714\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Aaron-2-by-Andrew-Jakus-1024x766.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Aaron-2-by-Andrew-Jakus-300x224.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Aaron-2-by-Andrew-Jakus-768x574.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Aaron-2-by-Andrew-Jakus.jpg 1079w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Courtesy Andrew Jakus</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Up the road from North Beach, North Point is another beloved destination among locals and visitors, including professional surfer <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@bengravyy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Ben Gravy</a> and Sheboyganite Aaron Renzelmann.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“I love to surf North Point just because of the energy, and when you’re out there, it’s such a rush. It’s so different than most of the other breaks around here,” Renzelmann said in <em>Dancing With Gravity</em>.  </p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The concept of Sheboygan as a surf destination was likely unfathomable to William Farnsworth, who first visited in 1814 and returned four years later to establish a fur trading post. Located at the mouth of the Sheboygan River on the western shore of Lake Michigan, the area had long been home to Native American tribes, including the Menominee, Ho-Chunk, Sauk, Fox, Ojibwe, and Potawatomi. </p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sheboygan-2-Photo-Credit-Larry-Williams-1024x680.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-78692\" srcset=\"https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sheboygan-2-Photo-Credit-Larry-Williams-1024x680.jpg 1024w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sheboygan-2-Photo-Credit-Larry-Williams-300x199.jpg 300w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sheboygan-2-Photo-Credit-Larry-Williams-768x510.jpg 768w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sheboygan-2-Photo-Credit-Larry-Williams-1536x1020.jpg 1536w, https://nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Sheboygan-2-Photo-Credit-Larry-Williams.jpg 2000w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">Courtesy of Larry Miller </figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">European settlers, many of them German, Dutch, or Irish immigrants drawn by farmland and other opportunities, began arriving in greater numbers in the 1840s. By the mid-19th century, the young city was home to a booming maritime industry, thanks to its abundant forests and strategic location for trade and commerce. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Sheboygan today is an outdoor lover’s paradise, with ample opportunity for water sports like kayaking, boating, and sailing, as well as hiking, biking, and golfing. Harms also shared the city’s other claim to fame: “We are the Bratwurst Capital of the World, and brat frys are plentiful in the area.”</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Local surfer Matt DeMaster perhaps sums up the waterfront destination’s appeal best: “It’s the perfect mix that everybody wants, which is [a] blue-collar, hardworking community that cares about each other, yet we have this kind of coastal vibe to us,” he said in <em>Dancing With Gravity</em>. “I don’t think there’s one thing that’s caused it, but it’s just a cool little spot.” </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">RELATED: <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/sports/seiichi-sano-worlds-oldest-surfer/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Meet the World’s Oldest Surfer: 89-Year-Old Seiichi Sano From Japan</a><br><br></p>\t\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/GettyImages-2251035526-1-scaled.jpg","t":"2026-09-08","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/6b10yftj.html":{"c":"<p>之前看到少数派会员说开会员就能给个Apple虚拟卡，我想着这东西是不是也不难，所以想着给所有我的小伙伴弄一个Apple虚拟卡。</p>\n<p>研究了一天，干了2.5亿token，终于是把Apple钱包的添加加进来了。（从头造轮子）</p>\n<p>所有HeoID用户均可添加哦。如果你在使用iOS27系统的iOS设备，那么将HeoID卡片添加进你的Apple钱包非常轻松。（旧版本系统也可以添加，只是样式不完整）</p>\n<p>首先进入<a href=\"https://id.zhheo.com/me?view=assets\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">我的资产</a>界面。点击添加按钮。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"添加卡片\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/1240920260901095941.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>然后打开相机扫一扫，如果使用微信扫码，需要使用默认浏览器打开。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"打开相机扫一扫\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/9841320260901100013.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>扫码后点击底部的添加到钱包按钮。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"添加到钱包\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/6316220260901102550.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>允许添加后即可在钱包App中看到啦！</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Apple 钱包\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/9340020260901102625.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<p>目前iOS27拥有此效果，较旧版本显示效果有所差异。</p>\n<p>赶快去试试吧！</p>\n<p>如果你是支持者会员，还有会员专属样式。</p>\n<h2 id=\"早鸟福利\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#早鸟福利\" title=\"早鸟福利\"></a>早鸟福利</h2><p>另外一些小伙伴看到我的文章速度很快，发个早鸟福利。</p>\n<p>进入<a href=\"https://id.zhheo.com/me?view=benefits\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">福利页面</a>点击右侧的兑换码兑换，使用下方的兑换码可以领取无限期的“先行者”主题卡面哦。（后续还有机会发，没领到也不用灰心）</p>\n<figure class=\"highlight plaintext\"><table><tr><td class=\"gutter\"><pre><span class=\"line\">1</span><br/><span class=\"line\">2</span><br/><span class=\"line\">3</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">6</span><br/><span class=\"line\">7</span><br/><span class=\"line\">8</span><br/><span class=\"line\">9</span><br/><span class=\"line\">10</span><br/></pre></td><td class=\"code\"><pre><span class=\"line\">2EC3WPESA5</span><br/><span class=\"line\">ABJD1HVEB</span><br/><span class=\"line\">MLHYFQ81</span><br/><span class=\"line\">N6NQ0VJY3DS</span><br/><span class=\"line\">QNYIK53L6QJY</span><br/><span class=\"line\">8MFLVD34</span><br/><span class=\"line\">AR80L3JD</span><br/><span class=\"line\">5W16H1MS</span><br/><span class=\"line\">LTXS95DSV</span><br/><span class=\"line\">4J6XW611V</span><br/></pre></td></tr></table></figure>\n<h2 id=\"Akilar群友福利\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Akilar群友福利\" title=\"Akilar群友福利\"></a>Akilar群友福利</h2><p>在Akilar糖果屋群的群友可以在群文件中找到兑换码文件（HeolD卡面兑换码.txt），兑换冰糖红茶主题卡面。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"冰糖红茶\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/6080020260902035710.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"支持者会员福利\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#支持者会员福利\" title=\"支持者会员福利\"></a>支持者会员福利</h2><p>支持本站发展的<a href=\"https://zhheo.com/sponsor/\" rel=\"noopener external nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">支持者会员</a>将会有会员专属卡面陪伴整个会员订阅期间。</p>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-11","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/wonderful-raises-550m-for-its-enterprise-ai-agent-platform/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>Wonderful has raised a $550 million Series C at a $5 billion valuation, led by Insight Partners. The company builds and runs AI agents for large enterprises, covering customer conversations across voice, chat, email, and in-app channels, employee requests that need action inside internal systems, and back-office work such as reconciling data and moving processes forward without a person involved. The platform is paired with full-stack engineering teams that sit inside customer environments in the market they serve, and that pairing is where the money is going.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>Teams build agents in plain language or in code, attach reusable skills, connect systems of record over API or MCP, and test variants side by side before shipping. Guardrails set what an agent can and cannot do, and full reasoning traces are recorded for every action, so an audit shows what an agent did and why. Live dashboards cover usage, efficiency, and outcomes. In January, the company shipped Agent Builder, an autonomous agent that builds, tests, and refines other agents, running on Anthropic's Claude.</p><p>Wonderful's stated position is that the hard part of enterprise AI is delivery. Agents that pass a demo still need integration into core systems, localization, compliance review, and continuous tuning, and enterprises pay for that gap in months of pilots that never carry live traffic. The company answers it by placing local teams inside customer environments, co-building with in-house staff and tuning agents to the language, regulation and operating context of each country. Wonderful says this moves deployments from pilot to production in days and weeks. ELTA Hellenic Post reports scaling agentic customer support by close to four times within two months of go-live, holding an 86 percent success rate in production.</p><p>Wonderful was founded in early 2025 by Bar Winkler and Roey Lalazar and came out of stealth that July. Twenty months on, it reports hundreds of agents, systems, and workflows running in production across a dozen verticals and more than 30 markets, including telecom, financial services, healthcare, and manufacturing. The round brings Salesforce in as a new investor, with Index Ventures, Bessemer, IVP, Vine Ventures and 9Yards returning. The capital is earmarked for customer delivery, hiring engineers and forward-deployed staff, and widening the product across the whole enterprise.</p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/09/wonderful.webp","t":"2026-09-05","p":"","n":0},"https://www.landian.news/archives/126640.html":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"content-post\">\n                <p class=\"excerpt color-border color-bg\">#è¡Œä¸šèµ„è®¯ æ»¡è¶³æ¬§ç›Ÿç½‘ç»œéŸ§æ€§æ³•æ¡ˆè¦�æ±‚ï¼šå¾®è½¯å®£å¸ƒä»�æ˜�å¹´ 3 æœˆå¼€å§‹é©±åŠ¨ç¨‹åº�æƒ³è¦�è�·å¾—å¾®è½¯ç­¾å��ï¼Œå¿…é¡»æ��ä¾› SBOM å’Œ VEXã€‚SBOM éœ€è¦�åˆ—å‡ºé©±åŠ¨ä½¿ç”¨çš„ç¬¬ä¸€æ–¹å’Œç¬¬ä¸‰æ–¹æ‰€æœ‰ç»„ä»¶ï¼ŒåŒ…æ‹¬åº“ã€�æ¡†æ�¶ã€�å·¥å…·ä»¥å�