¼Œå› æ­¤è¿™æ˜¯å¼ºåˆ¶æ€§æ”¿ç­–è€Œé��å�¯é€‰è®¤è¯�é¡¹ç›®ã€‚ç½‘ç»œéŸ§æ€§æ³•æ¡ˆè¦�æ±‚ç¡¬ä»¶å’Œè½¯ä»¶å¼€å�‘å•†æ�Œæ�¡äº§å“�ä¸­ä½¿ç”¨çš„ç¬¬ä¸‰æ–¹ç»„ä»¶ï¼Œåœ¨äº§å“�ç”Ÿå‘½å‘¨æœŸå†…æŒ�ç»­å¤„ç�†å®‰å…¨æ¼�æ´�å’Œä¾›åº”é“¾é£�é™©ã€‚</p>\n<p>å¾®è½¯è®¡åˆ’åœ¨ 2026 å¹´ 12 æœˆæ›´æ–° Windows Driver Kitï¼Œæ·»åŠ ç”Ÿæˆ�ã€�éªŒè¯� SBOM ä»¥å�Šåˆ¶ä½œ VEX å£°æ˜�çš„å·¥å…·ï¼ŒOEM ä¹Ÿå�¯ä»¥ä½¿ç”¨å…¶ä»–è¡Œä¸šå·¥å…·ï¼Œå�ªè¦�æœ€ç»ˆè¾“å‡ºæ»¡è¶³ SPDX 3.0 è§„èŒƒå�³å�¯ã€‚</p>\n<p>å�¦å¤– 2027 å¹´ 3 æœˆå‰�æ��äº¤çš„é©±åŠ¨ç¨‹åº�ä¸�ä¼šè¢«è¿½æº¯è¦�æ±‚æ��ä¾›æ��æ–™ï¼Œæ¯”è¾ƒæ—§çš„ Windows ç‰ˆæœ¬çš„è®¤è¯�è§„åˆ™ä¿�æŒ�ä¸�å�˜ï¼Œå�ªæœ‰ Windows æ–°ç‰ˆæœ¬æ‰�ä¼šæŒ‰ç…§è¦�æ±‚éœ€è¦�æ��ä¾›ç›¸å…³æ��æ–™ã€‚</p>\n<hr>\n<p>æ¶ˆæ�¯æº�ï¼š<a href=\"https://www.landian.news/go?url=https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/windows-hardware-certification/sboms-and-vex-statements-will-be-required-starting-032027/4552770?\" rel=\"nofollow\">Microsoft</a></p>\n<p class=\"single-activity-ticker\" aria-label=\"çƒ­é—¨æ�¨è��\"><a class=\"single-activity-link\" href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114184.html\" title=\"ä»…éœ€99å…ƒ/å¹´ï¼Œç¡…è°·CN2GIAæœ�åŠ¡å™¨ï¼Œå�¦æœ‰3å¹´ç‰ˆä»…éœ€528å…ƒï¼Œé™�é‡�é”€å”®ï¼Œå”®å®Œå�³æ­¢\"><span class=\"single-activity-label\">çƒ­é—¨æ�¨è��</span><span class=\"single-activity-window\"><span class=\"single-activity-track\"><span class=\"single-activity-title\">ä»…éœ€99å…ƒ/å¹´ï¼Œç¡…è°·CN2GIAæœ�åŠ¡å™¨ï¼Œå�¦æœ‰3å¹´ç‰ˆä»…éœ€528å…ƒï¼Œé™�é‡�é”€å”®ï¼Œå”®å®Œå�³æ­¢</span><span class=\"single-activity-title\" aria-hidden=\"true\">ä»…éœ€99å…ƒ/å¹´ï¼Œç¡…è°·CN2GIAæœ�åŠ¡å™¨ï¼Œå�¦æœ‰3å¹´ç‰ˆä»…éœ€528å…ƒï¼Œé™�é‡�é”€å”®ï¼Œå”®å®Œå�³æ­¢</span></span></span></a></p>            </div>\n        </div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-09-05","p":"","n":0},"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/5r2g9ie4.html":{"c":"<p>OpenClaw 8.1（官方叫 OpenClaw 2.0）发布快一个月了，这个版本改动大到离谱——16977 个 PR、987 个贡献者，基本上把整个项目重写了一遍。我从 RC 阶段就开始跟，踩了不少坑，尤其是记忆系统从 memory-lancedb-pro 迁移到 memory-core 这件事，记录一下。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"OpenClaw2.0\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/7313820260903034320.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"8-1-到底改了什么\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#8-1-到底改了什么\" title=\"8.1 到底改了什么\"></a>8.1 到底改了什么</h2><p>先说大面上的变化。</p>\n<h3 id=\"Session-存储迁移到-SQLite\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Session-存储迁移到-SQLite\" title=\"Session 存储迁移到 SQLite\"></a>Session 存储迁移到 SQLite</h3><p>最大的底层改动：会话和 transcript 从文件存储迁移到了 SQLite。官方专门加了降级警告——如果你从 8.1 回滚到旧版本，之前创建的 session 在旧版里看不到。升级前务必备份。</p>\n<h3 id=\"全新的引导式-Onboarding\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#全新的引导式-Onboarding\" title=\"全新的引导式 Onboarding\"></a>全新的引导式 Onboarding</h3><p>以前配 OpenClaw 得手动填 API key、选模型、配渠道，现在 Guided Setup 能自动检测你机器上已有的 Codex/ChatGPT/Claude CLI 登录状态，直接复用。Ollama 和 LM Studio 也能自动发现本地模型。 setup 完成后直接进第一个对话，不用再手动开终端。</p>\n<p>Mac 用户的体验改善最明显——应用从 Downloads 打开后会提示移到 Applications，更新和登录自启才正常工作。</p>\n<h3 id=\"Control-UI-大改\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Control-UI-大改\" title=\"Control UI 大改\"></a>Control UI 大改</h3><p>Web UI 重做了。现在 New Session 可以后台启动，不用等它加载完才能干别的。消息队列、中断恢复、跨 session 消息来源显示都做了。iPhone 上加了模型选择、权限控制、上下文管理这些 composer 控件。四种新主题可选。</p>\n<p>实际用下来最明显的感受是<strong>稳定性好了很多</strong>。旧版 WebUI 聊天时间一长就卡，长对话渲染慢、消息偶尔丢失，现在这些问题基本没了。SQLite 存储session之后，刷新页面不再丢上下文，切换 tab 也不用担心正在跑的请求断掉。</p>\n<p>配置项也多了不少。以前很多高级设置只能手动改 JSON，现在 WebUI 里直接能调——模型参数、权限控制、agent 配置、插件管理都有对应的界面。操作逻辑变了，比如 Settings 的布局重新组织过，Connection、Agent Identity、Plugins、Channels 这些原来散落在各处的功能现在归拢到一起了。刚上手会有点不适应，但找东西确实比以前快。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"配图\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/9633420260903042212.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<h3 id=\"Memory-系统重构\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Memory-系统重构\" title=\"Memory 系统重构\"></a>Memory 系统重构</h3><p>8.1 把 QMD（Quick Memory Database）正式退役，内置的 Memory Core 接管了核心搜索和召回路径。LanceDB、Memory Wiki、外部 embedding 服务、MEMORY.md、USER.md 各有分工，但核心检索逻辑统一了。</p>\n<p>新功能方面：个人 agent 默认开启跨对话记忆召回——你跟 agent 聊的内容，下次重置 session 后它还能想起来。前提是同一个 agent 的私聊，群聊和共享场景不受影响。Session 还支持 rewind 和 fork，可以从任意用户消息处回退，或者分叉出新对话分支。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"系统重构\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/0353420260903041504.jpg!blogimg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"为什么从-LanceDB-Pro-迁走\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#为什么从-LanceDB-Pro-迁走\" title=\"为什么从 LanceDB Pro 迁走\"></a>为什么从 LanceDB Pro 迁走</h2><p>说起来有点打脸——我之前还专门写过一篇文章推荐大家从 memory-core 换到 memory-lancedb-pro（<a href=\"https://blog.zhheo.com/p/0kl9erod.html%EF%BC%89%E3%80%82%E5%BD%93%E6%97%B6%E6%8E%A8%E8%8D%90%E7%9A%84%E7%90%86%E7%94%B1%E5%BE%88%E5%85%85%E5%88%86%EF%BC%9A\">https://blog.zhheo.com/p/0kl9erod.html）。当时推荐的理由很充分：</a></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>混合检索更精准</strong>：纯向量搜索召回不准，Pro 版用向量 70% + BM25 30% 混合权重 + Cross-Encoder 重排序，搜”删除”能精确命中那条铁律</li>\n<li><strong>智能提取和遗忘</strong>：LLM 自动分类六类记忆（profiles/preferences/entities/events/cases/patterns），Weibull 衰减让不重要记忆自然淡出</li>\n<li><strong>可控数据导入</strong>：4243 条记忆一键迁移，canonicalCorpus 自动索引，会话记录也能导入</li>\n</ul>\n<p>那篇文的结论是：”如果你想要更精准的语义检索、自动化的记忆管理、对记忆数据有完全控制权，memory-lancedb-pro 是目前最好的选择。”</p>\n<p>现在回头看，当时说的没错——<strong>在 8.1 之前</strong>，Pro 确实是更好的选择。memory-core 的纯向量检索确实有召回问题，我自己就是受害者。</p>\n<p>但 8.1 改变了整个游戏规则。</p>\n<p>我的环境之前用的是 memory-lancedb-pro + memory-wiki 组合。LanceDB Pro 有 4051 条活动记忆，占了 4.2GB 磁盘空间，用 bge-m3 做向量化（走 SiliconFlow API）。</p>\n<p>问题出在哪？</p>\n<p>LanceDB Pro 是第三方插件，每次 OpenClaw 大版本更新都得确认兼容性。8.1 把记忆核心重写了，Pro 的配置和 allowlist 留下一堆残留警告，Doctor 每次跑都报错。而且 8.1 之后 memory-core 是官方唯一推荐的核心检索路径，继续用第三方插件意味着官方的跨对话召回、rewind 这些新功能全用不上。</p>\n<p>再加上数据本身就很臃肿。导出一查重，2292 条跟 Markdown 文件重复，1196 条是库内互相重复，真正独有的只有 562 条。4GB 数据里六成是废的。</p>\n<h2 id=\"迁移过程\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#迁移过程\" title=\"迁移过程\"></a>迁移过程</h2><h3 id=\"去重是第一步\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#去重是第一步\" title=\"去重是第一步\"></a>去重是第一步</h3><p>直接迁移 4051 条记录到 memory-core 没意义，先把重复的干掉。</p>\n<p>我的做法：全量导出 LanceDB 数据，跟现有的 Markdown 文件做比对。比对维度是内容哈希 + 语义相似度（阈值 0.92）。结果：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>2292 条完全匹配已有 Markdown 文件</li>\n<li>1196 条在 LanceDB 库内互相重复</li>\n<li>562 条 confirmed 独有记忆</li>\n</ul>\n<p>这 562 条我按主题分了 6 个分类，整理成 Markdown 文件手动审核后并入 memory-core。有 1 条状态未知的记录，我没删，只保留在完整备份里。</p>\n<h3 id=\"验证必须做\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#验证必须做\" title=\"验证必须做\"></a>验证必须做</h3><p>迁移完不能直接跑。我的验证清单：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>memory-core 索引：1202/1202 文件、8842 chunks、Dirty=no</li>\n<li>向量检索：抽 3 组迁移过来的记忆做召回测试，全部命中</li>\n<li>FTS 全文搜索：正常</li>\n<li>Embedding 服务：SiliconFlow bge-m3 连接正常</li>\n<li>Wiki：259 个来源页，审计通过</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"回滚备份\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#回滚备份\" title=\"回滚备份\"></a>回滚备份</h3><p>备份放在单独的本地备份目录里，包含三样东西：完整配置备份、LanceDB 原始数据、全量导出的 JSON。万一迁移出问题，10 分钟能回滚。</p>\n<p><img alt=\"配图\" src=\"https://p.zhheo.com/5933020260903042408.png!blogimg\"/></p>\n<h2 id=\"踩过的坑\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#踩过的坑\" title=\"踩过的坑\"></a>踩过的坑</h2><h3 id=\"QMD-残留配置\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#QMD-残留配置\" title=\"QMD 残留配置\"></a>QMD 残留配置</h3><p>8.1 退役了 QMD，之前手动配过的参数会让 Doctor 报一堆警告。跑一遍 <code>openclaw doctor --fix</code> 能自动清理。但 QMD 独有的 reranking、query expansion、跨 agent transcript 搜索在新路径上没有替代，重度依赖的话迁移前得评估。</p>\n<h3 id=\"向量维度不兼容\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#向量维度不兼容\" title=\"向量维度不兼容\"></a>向量维度不兼容</h3><p>LanceDB Pro 默认的向量维度跟 memory-core 不一样。自定义 embedding 配了非标准维度的话，迁移直接报错。我迁移前用 <code>openclaw memory status --deep --agent main</code> 确认了 embedding 配置，没踩这个坑。</p>\n<h3 id=\"索引冲突\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#索引冲突\" title=\"索引冲突\"></a>索引冲突</h3><p>我遇到过一次索引冲突——升级过程中旧的 Memory Core 索引文件跟新的打架了。表现是 Gateway 启动失败，日志里报 “legacy Memory Core index conflicts”。解决方法：删掉旧索引文件让 memory-core 重新从 Markdown 重建。这个 bug 在后续的 8.2 里修了（#108652），但 8.1 用户得手动处理。</p>\n<h3 id=\"Active-Memory-时间戳格式\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Active-Memory-时间戳格式\" title=\"Active Memory 时间戳格式\"></a>Active Memory 时间戳格式</h3><p>如果你之前开了 Active Memory，它的 timestamp 格式在迁移过程中可能不兼容。malformed 的时间戳会阻塞整个迁移流程。解决方法：升级前先跑一遍 <code>openclaw memory index --force --agent main</code>，确保索引是干净的。</p>\n<h3 id=\"跨对话记忆的隐私边界\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#跨对话记忆的隐私边界\" title=\"跨对话记忆的隐私边界\"></a>跨对话记忆的隐私边界</h3><p>新功能默认开启跨对话召回，但只限同一个 agent 的私聊。群聊、频道消息、其他 agent 的对话不会被召回。这个设计合理，但要注意：如果你在多个 agent 之间共享了 MEMORY.md 或 Wiki，recall 的边界是 agent 级别而不是文件级别。别以为关了某个 agent 的对话就等于记忆消失了。</p>\n<h3 id=\"Skill-白名单问题\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Skill-白名单问题\" title=\"Skill 白名单问题\"></a>Skill 白名单问题</h3><p>升级后好几个 skill 不能用了，界面提示“需要设置”。查完发现不是缺依赖，是被 agent 白名单排除了。8.1 重构了 skill 加载逻辑，旧版白名单配置部分失效。<code>zhheo-blog-manager</code> 之前一直正常用，升级后直接变成 Excluded by agent allowlist。重新检查 <code>main</code> agent 的 <code>skills</code> 列表加回去就行。</p>\n<h3 id=\"明文凭据残留\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#明文凭据残留\" title=\"明文凭据残留\"></a>明文凭据残留</h3><p>升级体检发现配置里还有明文 API key，<code>openclaw secrets audit --check</code> 直接报 plaintext 警告。把明文凭据迁入 secret store 改成 SecretRef 就行。注意，模型配置文件是运行时生成物，不能手塞 SecretRef，会被审计判为 unresolved。旧的认证状态备份也可能含明文，需要一并检查和清理。</p>\n<h3 id=\"旧版插件兼容\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#旧版插件兼容\" title=\"旧版插件兼容\"></a>旧版插件兼容</h3><p><code>memory-lancedb-pro</code> 在 8.1 下还能跑，但配置残留和 allowlist 警告不断。我从 <code>plugins.allow</code> 移除了 <code>memory-core</code>（内置的不需要在 allow 列表里），给 <code>memory-lancedb-pro</code> 保留了 conversation hook 权限作为过渡。4GB 数据不能说丢就丢，先让旧插件跑着，等新环境稳定了再彻底清。</p>\n<h2 id=\"升级后的优化过程\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#升级后的优化过程\" title=\"升级后的优化过程\"></a>升级后的优化过程</h2><p>迁移只是第一步。升完级之后，一堆优化要做。</p>\n<h3 id=\"开启跨对话记忆召回\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#开启跨对话记忆召回\" title=\"开启跨对话记忆召回\"></a>开启跨对话记忆召回</h3><p>迁移完默认不开跨对话召回，官方保守设计，怕隐私问题。手动给 main agent 加了 <code>memory.search.rememberAcrossConversations</code>。开了之后效果很明显，reset session 后 agent 不再是“失忆”状态，上一个 session 聊的规则和偏好都能想起来。</p>\n<h3 id=\"配置-Active-Memory\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#配置-Active-Memory\" title=\"配置 Active Memory\"></a>配置 Active Memory</h3><p><code>active-memory</code> 也要手动启用。我用的配置是 <code>mode=escalate</code>、仅 main agent、仅 direct 对话、<code>persistTranscripts=false</code>。escalate 模式下 agent 主动判断哪些记忆值得写入，不无脑全存。persistTranscripts 关掉是因为会话记录自动索引太吵了，手动管理更可控。</p>\n<h3 id=\"Dreaming-定时任务\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Dreaming-定时任务\" title=\"Dreaming 定时任务\"></a>Dreaming 定时任务</h3><p>Dreaming 是 memory-core 的后台索引维护。设成每天凌晨 3:00（Asia/Shanghai）跑一次，新版不用显式声明 <code>light/rem/deep</code> 的 enabled 属性了。迁移后第一次完整 Dreaming 跑完，索引数据量正常。</p>\n<h3 id=\"Git-仓库瘦身\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#Git-仓库瘦身\" title=\"Git 仓库瘦身\"></a>Git 仓库瘦身</h3><p>升级后顺手跑了一遍 workspace 检查，发现 <code>.git</code> 里有一堆不该提交的东西——<code>.venv</code>、<code>.openclaw/state</code>、备份文件。dirty 状态从 19653 降到 1291，主要靠 <code>.gitignore</code> 补规则和把大文件从索引撤出。剩下的多是 memory/skills 历史堆积，没批量清理，影响不大。</p>\n<h3 id=\"备份策略调整\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#备份策略调整\" title=\"备份策略调整\"></a>备份策略调整</h3><p>旧的「每日备份」自动化用了 <code>find ... -delete</code>，违反删除铁律（必须进废纸篓），禁掉了。改用官方 Git 备份 + bundle：本机 <code>openclaw backup</code> 跑 Git 备份，再把 bundle 同步到远程存储。24 小时跑一次，已经验证过备份可以恢复，体积约 140M，不含 .venv 和敏感路径。</p>\n<h2 id=\"迁移后配置建议\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#迁移后配置建议\" title=\"迁移后配置建议\"></a>迁移后配置建议</h2><p>如果你也准备迁，这几项配置建议参考：</p>\n<ol>\n<li>main agent 开启 <code>memory.search.rememberAcrossConversations</code></li>\n<li>启用 <code>active-memory</code>，用 <code>mode=escalate</code>、仅 main、仅 direct、<code>persistTranscripts=false</code></li>\n<li>清理已禁用的 memory-lancedb-pro 配置和 allowlist 残留</li>\n<li>Dreaming 设成每天 03:00（Asia/Shanghai）</li>\n<li>Wiki 按需选 isolated 或 bridge 模式</li>\n<li><code>tools.sessions.visibility=all</code> 比默认宽，按需收紧</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"总结\"><a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#总结\" title=\"总结\"></a>总结</h2><p>OpenClaw 2.0 的记忆系统重构是一次迟早要来的收编。我之前推荐 LanceDB Pro 的理由——混合检索更精准、智能提取和遗忘、可控数据导入——在当时确实成立。但 8.1 把 QMD 退役、memory-core 接管核心路径之后，官方的跨对话召回、session rewind/fork 这些功能成了新的长期价值，第三方插件再好也追不上官方迭代节奏。</p>\n<p>迁移过程不算复杂，但去重和验证一定要做扎实，别直接把 4000 条记忆倒进去——六成是重复的，没意义。升完级之后的优化才是大头：白名单修复、凭据迁移、Active Memory 配置、备份策略调整……一步步来，别急。</p>\n<p>备份、验证、再验证。没了。</p>\n","i":"","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/google-releases-gemini-3-8-flash-and-flash-cyber/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>Google has released Gemini 3.8 Flash and Gemini 3.8 Flash Cyber, splitting its new model family between agentic work and restricted cyber defense. The third Flash launch in six weeks arrives three weeks after 3.7 Flash. Both variants share foundational intelligence, and 3.8 Flash keeps the same introductory pricing: $0.75 per million input tokens and $3.75 per million output tokens.</p><p>Gemini 3.8 Flash targets long-horizon coding, autonomous agents, and multi-step reasoning. Google says it beats most larger frontier models on DeepSWE v1.1 and scores 54.9% on HLE-Verified, with further gains on finance and legal agent benchmarks. Google attributes those results to additional reasoning steps and iterative tool calls. That can use more tokens at higher effort levels, so developers can select lower effort or stay on supported 3.7 Flash when compute efficiency matters.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>The model is available now through the Gemini API in Google AI Studio and Android Studio, plus Google Antigravity and Stitch. Enterprises can access it in Gemini Enterprise. Google AI Pro and Ultra subscribers can use it in the Gemini app, AI Mode in Search, and Gemini in Google Sheets.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>Gemini 3.8 Flash Cyber focuses on vulnerability discovery and automated patching. Google reports a success rate above 70% on an internal benchmark covering complex codebases in 20 languages. Its 47.2% pass@1 result on CWE-Bench trails a leading frontier modelâ€™s 47.8% at lower cost. Chromeâ€™s security team says it produced 2.6 times as many correct patches as the best commercial models tested. Wiz measured higher recall at lower cost, while Googleâ€™s Cloud Vulnerability Research team used it to find a critical foundational flaw in under two hours.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/tag/google/\">Google</a> says both releases were accelerated by long-running agentic loops that recursively evaluate and refine the models, with training advances that included cybersecurity work. Google limits cyber access to trusted government authorities, critical-infrastructure operators, and software maintainers through its new Fairwind Program. The Cyber variant uses more permissive cybersecurity mitigations, while the main Flash model carries safeguards for chemical, biological, radiological, nuclear, and cyber-offense risks under Googleâ€™s Frontier Safety Framework. The company also reports stronger prompt-injection robustness in Gray Swan testing.</p><p><a href=\"https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/models-and-research/gemini-models/3-8-flash-and-3-8-flash-cyber/?utm_source=x&amp;utm_medium=social&amp;utm_campaign=&amp;utm_content=\">Source</a></p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/09/banner-2.webp","t":"2026-09-06","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/icymi-openais-astra-crosses-critical-cybersecurity-threshold/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>OpenAI says Astra has crossed the Critical cybersecurity capability threshold under its Preparedness Framework, becoming the companyâ€™s first model at that level. With the right tools and access, Astra can find unknown flaws and develop working exploits across hardened systems without a person directing every step. OpenAI plans to release it soon, but its strongest cyber capabilities will first go to a small group of alpha testers, with Daybreak Blue access following for wider defensive use.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-embed-card\">\n</figure><p>OpenAI combined public and private benchmarks with expert-led tests. Astra scored 100% on ExploitBench and was substantially more capable and token-efficient than GPT-5.6 Sol in vulnerability discovery and exploit development. On an internal set of 20 recently disclosed high-severity V8 flaws, Astra delivered higher arbitrary-code-execution rates with far fewer output tokens. It also found two zero-days and used them in an exploit chain now being disclosed to maintainers. The results reflect Daybreak Blue access, not the default production setup.</p><p>In hands-on assessments, Astra built a browser compromise chain that escaped the sandbox and ran host commands when an HTML file was opened. It also combined flaws in a hardened operating system to escalate an unprivileged user to root. OpenAI says these results meet its Critical bar for zero-day exploitation across hardened systems or end-to-end attacks from a high-level goal.</p><p>OpenAI delayed parts of Astraâ€™s training and release while adding refusals, safety classifiers, offline detection, threat disruption, cross-conversation context handling, and monitoring that can stop unauthorized activity. Astra refused 91.5% of requests in cyber jailbreak evaluations, versus 59% for GPT-5.6 Sol. In honeypot tests based on the Hugging Face incident, Astra did not target surrounding systems or try to bypass auto-review denials.</p><p>For <a href=\"https://www.testingcatalog.com/tag/openai/\">OpenAI</a>, Astra is an early test of how its Preparedness Framework governs models capable of consequential work. The company says advanced access will expand cautiously as red-teaming, regression testing, and 24/7 response continue. Chain-of-thought monitoring will examine reasoning and actions for unauthorized behavior, while legitimate tasks may be slowed, paused, or stopped in ChatGPT, Codex, or the API. A system card at launch will provide more detail on Astraâ€™s safety, security, alignment, and evaluations.</p><p><a href=\"https://openai.com/index/path-to-astra/?ref=testingcatalog.com\">Source</a></p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/09/banner-1.webp","t":"2026-09-06","p":"","n":0},"https://www.mac52ipod.cn/post/byebye-tim-cook.php":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"textbox-content\" id=\"zoomtext\"><p>\n\t \t看我博客的人可能知道我不太喜欢 Tim Cook 这位苹果 CEO：这么多年，没做出来几个靠谱的新产品，甚至把老产品都差点搞砸了（参见最后那几年的英特尔处理器的 MacBook Pro，Mac Pro 好像也要被搞死了），大笔大笔的钱不去搞研发而是用做股票回购 ……</p><p>现在他离任了，终归得有个总结吧。正好看了何同学做的视频，推荐给大家吧：<u><a href=\"https://www.bilibili.com/video/BV1G7tG6tEwL/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"【何同学】库克时代\" rel=\"nofollow\"><font>【何同学】库克时代</font></a></u></p><p><a name=\"entrymore\"></a>\n</p>\n\t<p class=\"textbox-bottom\">\n\t</p>\n\t\n</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-09-12","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/lindy-can-now-schedule-meetings-from-email-thread/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>Lindy is an assistant that works inside email and calendar, and it has added a way to schedule meetings from the CC line. Adding the Lindy address to any thread where two people are trying to find a time hands off the coordination. Lindy reads what's already been said, pulls out the scheduling details, and fills in whatever is missing with sensible defaults.</p><p>From there, the behavior splits two ways. If the thread has already settled on a time, Lindy books it. If no time has been agreed, it replies once with three open slots as clickable links. The meeting lands on the calendar, and the invites go out. Everything the person on the other end has to do stays inside the email they were already reading, with no account or scheduling page required on their side. Constraints written in ordinary language in the thread are read and respected, so a line asking for mornings only or a thirty-minute call carries through without a settings screen.</p><p>Two conditions have to be true before anything happens. The Lindy address has to sit on the CC line, and the thread has to show that a time is actually being arranged. Where either is missing, the assistant stays out of the conversation.</p><p>Scheduling by CC has been possible in Lindy before this, but as a workflow that had to be assembled first. The published template walks through copying a dedicated Lindy mail address out of an email trigger, setting a condition that decides whether a time was proposed or still needs searching, configuring a calendar action with working hours and daily meeting caps, and writing the reply text the assistant sends back. This release reaches the same outcome without that build, moving scheduling from something configured in advance to behavior that runs on the thread itself.</p><p>Lindy was founded in 2023 by Flo Crivello, previously a product manager at Uber and founder of the virtual office company Teamflow. The assistant already runs across several surfaces. It works in Gmail through a Chrome extension, answers inside Slack channels and direct messages, runs from iMessage, and joins calls on Meet, Zoom, and Teams to record and file notes into folders described in plain language. It connects to Gmail, Drive, Calendar, and Notion, plus more than a thousand other integrations; supports MCP servers; and keeps its memory in plain files that can be opened and edited. Anything carrying outside consequences waits on approval from a named person, the same guardrail that governs the scheduling flow. Plans start at 29.99 dollars per user per month, with SOC 2 Type II, GDPR, and PIPEDA compliance reported, and HIPAA available on the enterprise tier.</p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/09/Lindy-CC.jpg","t":"2026-09-07","p":"","n":0},"https://www.v2ex.com/t/1239398":{"c":"<div class=\"topic_content\">0.5%å�«æš´æ¶¨-3%å�«å¾®è°ƒ</div>\n<hr/><div class=\"subtle\">\n<span class=\"fade\">Supplement 1  Â·  <span title=\"2026-09-04 11:21:31 +08:00\">21h 6m ago</span></span>\n<div class=\"sep5\"></div>\n<div class=\"topic_content\">0.5%å�«æš´æ¶¨-3%å�«å¾®è°ƒ</div>\n</div>\n<hr/><h3>评论</h3>\n<p><strong>#1 IceSolStice</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">è´¹å�Šå¾®æ¶¨-&gt;éŸ©å’•å™œæ¶¨-&gt;å¤§ A å°�æ¶¨</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#2 QingXuJiaZhi</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">æ˜¨å¤©è¶…è·Œ+ç¾�è‚¡å¤§æ¶¨</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#3 quan01994</strong>：<div class=\"reply_conte