<p class=\"excerpt color-border color-bg\">#系统资讯 Linux Kernel 7.1 系列最终版发布：Linux Kernel 7.1.13，至此 7.1 全系列结束生命周期支持。内核团队建议用户立即升级 7.2 系列，不过下游发行版通常维护自己的内核版本并移植补丁。所以用户需要查询使用的发行版网站，看看当前的内核支持状态。查看全文：https://ourl.co/126682</p><p>Linux Kernel 7.1 系列已经结束生命周期不再提供任何安全更新，该版本最初是在 2026 年 6 月 14 日发布的，由于 7.1 系列并非 LTS 长期支持版因此生命周期非常短。</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2023/08/99983.png\" data-fancybox=\"gallery\" rel=\"nofollow\"><img fetchpriority=\"high\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone\" src=\"https://img.lancdn.com/landian/2023/08/99983.png\" alt=\"Linux Kernel 7.1已经结束生命周期不再提供更新 用户应尽快升级到7.2系列\"></a></p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<p>在整个 7.1 系列里共有 13 个稳定版维护更新，最终版本为 9 月 2 日发布的 Linux Kernel 7.1.13 版，该版本包含 76 项修复，涉及 KVM、USB、音频、WiFi、文件系统和加密等组件。</p>\n<p>结束生命周期后内核团队不再提供任何错误修复和安全更新，官方建议仍然使用该分支的用户应该尽快迁移到 Linux Kernel 7.2 系列。如果不想频繁更新内核则可以考虑迁移到 Linux Kernel LTS 系列。</p>\n<p>这种非长期支持版属于 Linux 普通稳定内核的常见维护方式，普通版本会在新版本发布后结束维护，只有被选为长期支持的版本才会获得更长的支持周期。</p>\n<p><strong><div class=\"message-box message-style module-radius success\"><p class=\"salong-message-content\"> 最新稳定版为 Linux Kernel 7.2.3：</p></div></strong></p>\n<p>Linux Kernel 7.2 系列在 2026 年 8 月 16 日发布，目前稳定版更新已经到 7.2.3 版，所以内核团队也建议使用 7.2 系列的用户升级到 7.2.3 版，新版本修复大量已知错误和安全问题。</p>\n<p>需要区分上游内核与下游 Linux 发行版内核，像是 Ubuntu、Debian、RHEL 等发行版通常会自行维护所使用的内核并移植安全补丁，因此系统显示的版本低于 7.2 不代表已经停止安全更新，所以用户应当查询发行版网站确认内核支持信息。</p>\n<p><strong></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Linux Kernel 6.18</li>\n<li>Linux Kernel 6.12</li>\n<li>Linux Kernel 6.6</li>\n<li>Linux Kernel 6.1</li>\n<li>Linux Kernel 5.15</li>\n<li>Linux Kernel 5.10</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"single-activity-ticker\" aria-label=\"热门推荐\"><a class=\"single-activity-link\" href=\"https://www.landian.news/archives/114184.html\" title=\"仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止\"><span class=\"single-activity-label\">热门推荐</span><span class=\"single-activity-window\"><span class=\"single-activity-track\"><span class=\"single-activity-title\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span><span class=\"single-activity-title\" aria-hidden=\"true\">仅需99元/年，硅谷CN2GIA服务器，另有3年版仅需528元，限量销售，售完即止</span></span></span></a></p>            </div>\n        </div></body></html>","i":"","t":"2026-09-08","p":"","n":0},"https://nicenews.com/culture/start-book-club-sample-reading-list/":{"c":"<html><body><div><div class=\"entry-content clear\" ast-blocks-layout=\"true\" itemprop=\"text\">\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">There’s arguably never been a better time to join a book club. According to reading subscription service <a href=\"https://fable.co/blog/2026-state-of-reading-report\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Everand’s 2026 State of Reading Report</a>, people read more often last year than they did the year prior and in multiple formats, as e-books and audiobooks abound — and they’re primarily discovering new recs through personal connections. And considering the importance of <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/health-and-wellness/third-place-boosts-your-mental-health/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">third places</a>, a book club is the perfect way to dive into a new read <em>and</em> build community at the same time.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">“[Book clubs] open up this idea that we can now all sit together and talk about this book and enjoy this moment together, while also then allowing ourselves to go forth into the world feeling like we’ve learned something,” New York City book club founder Zoë Mahler <a href=\"https://www.nbcnews.com/pop-culture/pop-culture-news/book-clubs-social-scenes-gen-z-millennials-rcna200328\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">told</a> NBC News. </p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">And perhaps the best part? These events have evolved far beyond the traditional version of simply sitting in a circle in someone’s living room (although those still exist, too!). So if you’re craving a certain type of literary gathering and not finding it in your area, why not create it yourself? </p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-how-to-start-a-book-club\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Start a Book Club</h2>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-choose-your-own-adventure\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Choose Your Own Adventure</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Since book clubs can be launched in all kinds of creative formats, take some time to consider the experience you’d like to curate. Do you want it to be in-person or online? At someone’s house, or in a public location like a park or brewery? Should the conversation be entirely centered on a single book each meeting, or is bonding over a shared love of reading what’s most important?</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">To get the juices flowing, here are some different types of book clubs you might want to try:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Silent: Bring your own book, read quietly together, then socialize (or not)</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Book swap: Bring a book to give away, browse others’ contributions, and mingle with readers</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Hobby-related: Combine discussions with events incorporating other shared interests, such as art, running, baking, or gardening</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Virtual: Host literary discussions through Zoom or a similar platform, and invite speakers or authors to present</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<blockquote class=\"instagram-media\" data-instgrm-captioned data-instgrm-permalink=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DXkLA7UiQxN/?utm_source=ig_embed&amp;utm_campaign=loading\" data-instgrm-version=\"14\"></blockquote>\n\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-specify-a-genre-or-theme\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Specify a Genre or Theme</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Depending on the vibe of your club, you may want to narrow its focus by selecting books that fall within a specific genre or topic. If you’re just looking to bring people together to socialize over a mutual passion for reading, you can bounce around a little here — but if you’d like to center the books themselves and attract a like-minded group, feel free to niche down a bit.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You could pick a broad genre like general romance or thriller, or go with something more specific like romantasy, LGBTQ+ romance, <a href=\"https://kristenvannest.com/2026/03/15/wellness-cult-thrillers-books/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">wellness-cult thriller</a>, or cowboy romance (yes, those last two are a thing!). Alternatively, you may want to only read recent <em>New York Times</em> bestsellers, award-winning works, cookbooks, novels with a specific setting (like Japan), or nonfiction titles that cover a specific topic (such as mental health). And as your club gets going, you could implement a voting system to choose each month’s read. </p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-work-out-logistics\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Work Out Logistics</h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">As fun as it is to have finally decided you’re going to only discuss ’80s vampire novels, now comes the perhaps less exciting but entirely necessary part: Establishing a functional club. Here are a few questions you’ll want to answer:</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1307240916-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-77119\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1307240916-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1307240916-300x200.jpg 300w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1307240916-768x512.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1307240916-1536x1025.jpg 1536w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1307240916-2048x1367.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">g-stockstudio/iStock</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>How often will the club meet?</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Who will host? Will it be you every time, or will you rotate hosting duties?</li>\n\n\n\n<li>How large do you want it to be?</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Where will everyone meet, and what do you need to do to make that happen (reserve a table at a wine bar, book a room at a library, etc.)?</li>\n\n\n\n<li>How will you communicate with members (through social media, email, text, or something else)?</li>\n\n\n\n<li>What other things do you need to prepare for the event (for example, snacks at your house or a route for a post-discussion run)?</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In terms of inviting members, there are several avenues you can take. If you have a few interested friends, you can ask each of them to <em>also </em>bring a few friends and go from there — or, you can use a website like <a href=\"https://bookclubs.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Bookclubs</a> to build in-person groups in your area. Social media tools, like Facebook groups or TikTok posts, are another great way to get the word out. And if you’re starting an online club, platforms such as Bookclubs and <a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/group?ref=nav_comm_groups\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Goodreads</a> offer ways to do this via virtual message boards, as well as meeting apps like Zoom.</p>\t\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-create-a-cadence-nbsp-nbsp\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Create a Cadence  </h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">No matter what type of book club you’re launching, you’ll want to have some sort of structure in place, particularly for the first meeting or if your members don’t know each other. If you’re following a more traditional literary discussion format, here’s a <a href=\"https://bookriot.com/book-club-discussion-questions/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">general list</a> of questions to get you started, as well as <a href=\"https://www.litlovers.com/run-a-book-club/lead-a-book-club-discussion\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">ideas</a> for generating fun conversation. But if you’d prefer more book-specific prompts, check out <a href=\"https://www.bookbrowse.com/reading_guides/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">BookBrowse</a> or <a href=\"https://www.readinggroupguides.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Reading Group Guides</a>, which offer free guides for thousands of titles.</p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" src=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1132787678-1024x683.jpg\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-77121\" srcset=\"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1132787678-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1132787678-300x200.jpg 300w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1132787678-768x512.jpg 768w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1132787678-1536x1024.jpg 1536w, https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1132787678-2048x1365.jpg 2048w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\"><figcaption class=\"wp-element-caption\">SolStock/iStock</figcaption></figure>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">But remember, there’s no need to stick to a specific cadence — in fact, some relaxed clubs don’t even require attendees to actually <em>read</em> the book. Still, it’s a good idea to nail down the guidelines and flow of your event, and share it ahead of time so everyone knows what to expect.</p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h2 id=\"h-ready-to-read\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Ready to Read?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Naturally, what you choose to read depends on the genre or theme of your club, but we’ve rounded up a list of books to help you get started, some of which are top-clicked titles previously included in editions of Nice News.</p>\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-fiction\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Fiction</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"></p>\n\n\n\n<h3 id=\"h-nonfiction\" class=\"wp-block-heading\">Nonfiction</h3>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">RELATED: <a href=\"https://nicenews.com/lifestyle/best-books-april-reading-list-2023/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Nice News’ Reading List: 11 of Our Favorite Books Released in April</a></p>\t\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>When you buy books through our links, Nice News may earn a commission, which helps keep our content free</em>.</p>\n\n\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://inbox-media-offload.nicenews.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/iStock-1389876849.jpg","t":"2026-09-09","p":"","n":0},"https://www.v2ex.com/t/1239824":{"c":"<div class=\"topic_content\">æœ¬äººæ²¡æœ‰è¯»è¿‡å¤§å­¦ï¼Œå­¦å�†é��å…¨æ—¥åˆ¶å¤§ä¸“å’Œé��å…¨æ—¥åˆ¶æœ¬ç§‘ï¼Œè¿�ç»´ç›¸å…³å·¥ä½œï¼Œå·¥ä½œæ�¥è¿‘ 7 å¹´ï¼Œä¸€å…±åœ¨ä¸‰ä¸ªå…¬å�¸å¾…è¿‡ï¼Œè¿›è¿‡ä¹™æ–¹å¤§å�‚ï¼Œéƒ½æ˜¯é©»åœºç”²æ–¹å·¥ä½œã€‚è®ºæŠ€æœ¯æˆ‘ä¸�æ¯”åˆ«äººå·®ï¼Œé��å¤–åŒ…å·¥ä½œæˆ‘ä¹Ÿæ‰¾è¿‡ï¼Œé�¢è¯•éƒ½èƒ½è¿‡ï¼Œæœ‰å››ä»½å·¥ä½œéƒ½æ˜¯ä¸‹ offer å��äº¤èµ„æ–™æˆ–è€…èƒŒè°ƒè¢« pass äº†ã€‚æˆ‘è¿™ä¸ªå­¦å�†æ˜¯ä¸�æ˜¯å�ªæœ‰å¹²å¤–åŒ…çš„å‘½äº†ï¼Œæˆ‘æœ¬äººå¯¹å¤–åŒ…å€’æ˜¯ä¸�å¤ªä»‹æ„�ï¼Œå·¥èµ„ç»™å¤Ÿå°±è¡Œ</div>\n<hr/><h3>评论</h3>\n<p><strong>#1 PrinceofInj</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">çœ‹è¡Œä¸šï¼Œä¹Ÿ