½ä¼ åˆ°æœ�åŠ¡å™¨ä¸Šäº†</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#72 vanxy</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">æ”¹äº†ä¸�ä¸€å®šä¼šé…�ï¼Œå¾ˆå¤šéƒ½æ˜¯ç½‘ä¸Šæ‰¾çš„æ•™ç¨‹ï¼Œ é…�é”™äº†ï¼Œç½‘æ��ç‚¸äº†è¿˜å¾—æ‰¾å¸ˆå‚…ä¿®ï¼Œå¸ˆå‚…å«Œéº»çƒ¦</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#73 S0lution</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">å�¯èƒ½çœ‹äººï¼Ÿä¸Šå‘¨åˆšè£…çš„ï¼Œæ±Ÿè‹�ç§»åŠ¨æ�¢ç”µä¿¡ï¼Œå¸ˆå‚…çœ‹æˆ‘å¼±ç”µç®±é‡Œä¸€ä¸ªå…‰çŒ«ä¸€ä¸ªç›’å­�ï¼Œç›´æ�¥é—®æˆ‘è¦�ç»™ä½ æ”¹æ¡¥æ�¥å�—ï¼Ÿæˆ‘è¯´ è¦�ï¼Œé¡ºä¾¿èƒ½æŠŠå…‰çŒ«è¶…çº§å¯†ç �ç»™æˆ‘å˜›ï¼Œå¸ˆå‚…è¯´ è¡Œ</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#74 Sezxy</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">è·Ÿç»´ä¿®çš„æ��å¥½å…³ç³»ï¼Œæˆ‘æŠ•è¯‰è�”é€šçš„å…‰çŒ«æ²¡æœ‰ 2.5G å�£å��ï¼Œç»´ä¿®å¸ˆå‚…ç›´æ�¥æŠŠ Loid ç»™æˆ‘ï¼Œè®©æˆ‘è‡ªå·±æ�¢ä¸ªç¬¬ä¸‰æ–¹çš„å…‰çŒ«</div></p><hr/>","i":"","t":"2026-09-07","p":"","n":0},"https://www.testingcatalog.com/metas-muse-agent-enters-closed-alpha-with-invite-codes/":{"c":"<html><body><div><section id=\"post-body\" class=\"post-body godo-canvas mx-auto relative font-serif\">\n        \n\n    <p>Meta’s upcoming AI agent, Muse, appears to be moving closer to launch. Earlier, we reported that Muse would be accessible through a waitlist, but several details have changed since then. In addition to the waitlist, Meta will introduce invite codes that users can distribute to help others gain access. The agent also seems to have moved from internal testing into a closed alpha phase, with limited regional availability that is very likely restricted to \"Saint Kitts and Nevis\" for now.</p><p>Based on what is currently known about the waitlist page, mobile apps and a web version will be available at launch. A desktop version will likely follow later. We have also recently gained access to the application’s description and several early screenshots.</p><p>The description reads: <em>“Muse is your personal AI agent that gets things done, always working on what matters to you. It manages email, books dinners, tracks budgets, and finds deals with your approval.”</em></p><p>Also, <em>“Muse takes the busy work off your plate. It manages scheduling conflicts, books reservations, sets reminders, and follows up with people so birthdays, plans, and deadlines don't slip. Stay on top of your calendar, email, and daily tasks without carrying it all in your head.”</em></p><p>Based on this description, Meta appears to be targeting cliché tasks such as booking tables. The more interesting promise, however, is that Muse will sit on top of a user’s calendar, email, and daily tasks. If Meta builds it as an assistant focused purely on task execution and designs the UI around that purpose, Muse could become a much bigger play. Competition in this space is already fierce, but there is still a massive opportunity to do it much better.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-gallery-card kg-width-wide kg-card-hascaption\"><figcaption><p><span>Muse UI</span></p></figcaption></figure><p>The first screenshot, “Your personal agent that takes things off your plate,” shows a standard chat interface with an avatar of the Muse character at the top. The avatar uses light brown tones and looks a little childish, while remaining serious enough to fit the overall design. The prompt bar is also standard, complete with an attachment button and a dictation voice icon. In the featured example, Muse finds a travel document, offers to sign it, and sends a confirmation email, which the user accepts. Muse also sends an emoji reaction to show that it has started working on the task. If the agent is genuinely proactive like this, it will be a big deal.</p><p>The next screenshot, “Approve what gets sent or spent,” focuses on user authorization. Muse says, “Found a few travel strollers for Luca, perfect for your trip,” displays the price, and asks whether the user is interested. It then presents a widget where the user can select a payment method, view the details, and authorize the transaction.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-gallery-card kg-width-wide kg-card-hascaption\"><figcaption><p><span>Muse UI</span></p></figcaption></figure><p>“Track ticket prices and book reservations” shows one of the interface's more distinctive parts: an interactive browser-window widget that the user can open as a link. Muse uses it to open a cinema website, select seats, and handle the booking. The browser widget also carries a “Beta” label.</p><p>The “Connect the apps you already use” screenshot displays connectors for Gmail, Google Calendar, HealthX, OpenTable, Facebook, Instagram, Peloton, Plaid, and Function Health. This selection indicates that Muse will support health, fitness, and financial integrations alongside communication, scheduling, and reservation services.</p><p>Another screen, “Get ideas for what your agent can take on,” presents several suggested prompts: “I can follow up on your airplane refund,” “I can find a bigger stroller for Luca,” “Build a daily training plan for your half marathon,” “I can book your anniversary dinner,” and “I can help dial in your sleep.” If Muse is proactive or at least provides a dedicated tab for browsing these kinds of ideas, this part of the product could be very interesting.</p><figure class=\"kg-card kg-gallery-card kg-width-wide kg-card-hascaption\"><figcaption><p><span>Muse UI</span></p></figcaption></figure><p>The final screenshot, “Understand your spending and find ways to save,” begins with a prompt directly from the user asking Muse to review their spending. The next screen says, “Turn your goals into a real plan.” It includes a to-do list with different goals and checkboxes that users can modify and check off. The “create goal” area includes sections for health and relationships, with probably more sections underneath that are not currently visible.</p><p>This is the latest set of findings on top of what was discovered earlier. Many more features will likely be added to Muse gradually, but it is already clear that the agent is undergoing testing with a closed group of users on mobile and web. A desktop version could potentially arrive soon as well. </p><p><strong>Source:</strong> Apple's App Store currently exposes a <a href=\"https://apps.apple.com/kn/app/muse-from-meta/id6760173601?ref=testingcatalog.com\">Meta-authored listing</a> for \"Muse from Meta\". It also describes finance, fitness, shopping, background work, activity log, connector control, and customization capabilities.</p>\n</section>\n\n\n\n\n</div></body></html>","i":"https://storage.ghost.io/c/2a/1b/2a1b1782-8506-4d7d-bf53-ad3fb52e2a0f/content/images/size/w1200/2026/09/Muse-from-Meta-09-06-2026_11_08_PM-1.jpg","t":"2026-09-09","p":"","n":0},"https://www.v2ex.com/t/1239961":{"c":"<div class=\"topic_content\">最近跟人起了纠纷，对方声称能通过所谓的“三网定位”实时获取我的位置。目前的情况让我怀疑，对方可能确实掌握了我的位置信息，现在有点惶恐。<br/>但我不了解这方面的技术，也没法确认对方到底用了什么手段，是不是真的能持续、实时定位，还是通过其他渠道获得信息后拿来吓唬我。<br/>想请教一下了解通信、隐私安全的朋友：<br/>1. 所谓的“三网定位”到底是什么？普通人真的能仅凭手机号查到别人的实时位置吗？<br/>2. 如何排查位置泄露的来源，区分是手机或账号的问题、共享定位没关，还是其他渠道泄露？<br/>3. 如果怀疑是手机号相关的信息泄露，有哪些实际有效的防范措施？换号码、换 SIM 卡或者换手机有没有意义？<br/>4. 这种情况应该保留哪些证据，向运营商投诉是否有用？<br/>不求查询渠道，也不想反查对方，只想搞清楚风险、保护自己。涉及个人隐私和纠纷的细节暂时不方便公开，希望有经验的朋友指点一下，谢谢。</div>\n<hr/><h3>评论</h3>\n<p><strong>#1 bluehr</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你自己是程序员还能被这么低级的话给唬住吗？</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#2 zljklang</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">我告诉你你把，叔叔都只能定位到范围。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#3 hooych</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">电话录音，问问对方要多少钱，直接打钱过去</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#4 ImINH</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">不算吓唬吧，只要花钱确实可以，应该基站三角定位吧，基于运营商基站的信号强度。手机号关机就行了，没啥。但实际上这样查的成本也是很高的，我不确定你说的对方有能力负担。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#5 Nasdaq</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">这么牛批，给国服一号定位一下。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#6 IlIl</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你说你会脑控，他再骚扰你，你就远程控制他的 jj 爆炸</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#7 Promtheus</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你就说你已经用星链锁定他了 马上给普京一个电话核导弹就到他家。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#8 cz5424</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你这纠纷的金额有点大把，还值得三网定位</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#9 coderluan</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">讲道理，即使你真信了，不去报警去投诉运营商？</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#10 bluehr</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/IlIl\">IlIl</a> 哈哈哈，厉害。一个控制他在 xx 的时候爆炸，把隧道堵死</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#11 jackOff</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你去中国暗网：小黄鱼里看看有没有营业厅的搞这种权力变现</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#12 77158158</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">这个好像是社工内的。<br/>三网基站定位（全网独家）<br/>用法: /dw 手机号<br/>示例: /dw 13800138000<br/>费用: 普通用户 20 积分 / 会员 10 积分</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#13 Vegetable</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">运营商以前可以，现在管理严了不知道，当然准确性肯定不是 gps 级别</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#14 InDom</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">通过运营商基站获取手机卡定位, 精度大概几百米的样子, 是个范围, 技术理论是没问题的, 公开成熟.<br/><br/>但是, 对方说能定位你, 这个事存疑.<br/><br/>明确能通过基站定位的, 只有你的手机(及 APP)与运营商能获取到.<br/><br/>通过你手机方面泄漏的可能性不大, 对方能通过运营商方面获取到你的定位, 这个事不能说没可能.<br/><br/>而且, 通过运营商获取你的定位, 首先对方得知道你的手机号码.<br/><br/>这种查询肯定不是普通人随随便便就能查的. 你得捅多大的篓子啊, 值得这么对待?</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#15 Yuunie</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">运营商确实可以通过两个或多个信号塔确定用户的大概位置，但这东西普通人也不能随便查啊，直接报警</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#16 Arei</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">我寻思，三网定位还是一定范围内的，真的要定位你，不应该直接查你手机绑定的身份/地址信息吗，这些信息泄露也严重多了吧，光三网定位就让他去猜呗</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#17 mathiashu4</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">确实可以被基站定位，但是看起来你不值得。应该只是打嘴炮</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#18 ala2008</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">有。不过成本应该很高</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#19 Alloyt</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你要恭喜他，他找到了一个带编制的工作了</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#20 PopRain</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">如果你开车，偷偷给你车上贴个跟踪器就能跟踪，磁吸的，很难发现；或者扔一个 apple tag , 你不用苹果手机也很难发现</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#21 williampan</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">我觉得你先搞清楚你手机号码在手机里关机后，会到路过基站报道否？如果会那这种报道是记录卡号还是设备号，还是一块记录？弄清楚你就该有清晰框架了。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#22 karmaisbitch</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">基站定位也就是一个范围，有什么好怕的，以前都是用来布控重点人群的</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#23 yinmin</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">4G/5G 基站对手机定位，如果手机在室外是很准的，精度可以在 20 米以内，如果手机在室内大概小几百米。但是这个不开放给公众的，普通人是查不到的。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#24 Fish1024</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">楼上这么多说不行或者成本太高的，忘记那几年你出个门就红码了？<br/>不要高估运营商内工作人员的职业道德。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#25 zt5b79527</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/Arei\">Arei</a> 这个逻辑靠谱。如果真有能量，直接从手机号就能查到家庭住址详细信息了，所以这个“三网定位”应该只有两种可能，一种就是纯唬人的，一种就是用非法手段从运营商后台获取的大致定位。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#26 tcper</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">现在信息泄露那么普遍，想获取位置太容易了，随便一个辅警都可以查询</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#27 nunterr</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">三网定位：只有运营商可以，只要知道你的手机号就可以做，不论你是否换手机卡只要你开机都能定位到你，如果是普通人他说可以三网定位或者其他监控定位，那你就可以报警了如果查到他是公职人员搞得最起码他能背个处分，其他方式定位：如果存网络你别点击各种链接，手机厂商的云定位，其他的就是各种小设备的定位，这种会被放到车辆，或者你的常用的设备中，注意好这些基本上没啥问题</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#28 gpt5</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">v 我 100 ，我通过三网定位给你反定位他。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#29 wenrouxiaozhu</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/77158158\">77158158</a> #12 20 积分就可以？这么便宜</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#30 ClaudeCode</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">sgk 随便搞啊， 只要知道你的手机号。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#31 bunai</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你是干啥了，你怕啥</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#32 xixiv5</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">基站定位 花钱就行</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#33 Cruzz</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">telegram 随便找个社工库问老板多少钱，给钱没有办不到的。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#34 maplezzz</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">定位你然后呢，他还能过来砍你吗</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#35 willwon1</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">统一回复一下 、对方已经实际说出了我的实际定位地址、我的居住楼层单元</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#36 frankies</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">当然可以，只要肯花钱买，让叔叔用警务通一查就出来了，什么位置啊最新的快递外卖地址啊社保工作单位啊都行的。他能查你，你也能查他，你怕个毛啊</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#37 jakson</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">基站能查到一个范围，大概几百米到几公里</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#38 frankies</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a> 你有理就报警吧，把聊天截图给帽子，让他们在警务系统里查调取你信息的历史记录，抓内鬼去。他购买公民个人信息罪加一等。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#39 bitmin</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">定位了又能怎么样？他愿意付出多大代价搞你？他敢搞你你敢不敢搞他？<br/><br/>这种人都是怂人，狠人有仇当场就报了，哪里会打嘴炮这样哔哔<br/><br/>如果是网络上打嘴炮更简单了，拿着网络通讯记录去派出所备案，并记录下来发给他，通常这时候他就吓尿了</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#40 jackOff</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a> 牛逼，直接报警抓这种虎逼啊，现在严打灰产，这种只可能是内部人员出问题了，参考江西警方内部售卖警务通查询直接坐牢的例子</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#41 Desdemor</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a>  看着像是开盒，也不是也实时的轨迹啊，你说的怪吓人的，你现在跑到派出所，他要还能定位你，正好报警</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#42 abc1310054026</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">知道你手机号就行以及肯花钱就行了，遗憾的是你没办法，除非你换手机换房子。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#43 moefishtang</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/Yuunie\">Yuunie</a> 运营商甚至还卖这种业务...电信有个亲情守护（还是别的名字，忘了），就是可以查询授权手机号的基站定位信息...(以前移动有个亲情通也是类似的），不过这个开通要对方授权</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#44 lyc776</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">这不就是开盒么，哪需要这么复杂，还三网定位。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#45 bunai</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a> 你被开盒了</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#46 MindMindMax</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">成本问题。如果不是电诈，还是和谈吧。人家觉得搞你值得那么多成本，就一定会搞你。<br/>如果你有车子的话，没准你车子上装了 GPS 也不好说。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#47 Wyearn</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">可以定位，但是好像误差是 500 米吧。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#48 andyskaura</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a> 这是社工库查的记录吧，三网定位也定不到楼层单元</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#49 BUCKS</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">听着好兴奋，可以反 hack 他全家啊</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#50 ala2008</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a> 这个是基于外卖快递这些来的</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#51 willwon1</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/andyskaura\">andyskaura</a> 我刚好去外地、这里的定位地址我没有任何外卖记录、实时轨迹</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#52 Smileh</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你直接 110 不行吗？</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#53 liubai256</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a> #51 铁了心要弄你还是直接报警吧，灰产渠道现在到处都是成本不低的，这么嚣张还舍得花钱你是偷他钱了还是咋他了</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#54 Rickkkkkkk</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">可以做到的。<br/><br/>建议你报警。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#55 cz5424</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a> 你这个更简单了，开盒酒店记录是比较多的</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#56 yougg</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">有没有可能是更现实的方式: 对方线下找人盯梢你了</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#57 catning</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">报出你居住地址的时候，你已经立于不败之地了。害怕啥呀～</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#58 loading</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">你直接说：是吗？我回去问下我 xx 叔，他公安局的应该知道你说的是不是真的。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#59 zhangli2946</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">“明天去缅北了，这是我的地址。来找我，如果你找到我，我就让你...嘿嘿嘿”</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#60 datocp</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">当年只知道考生手机不通，同事竟然通过熟人关系帽子的系统联系到了考生。。。<br/>也许有些人有权限接触到什么特别的系统。<br/><br/>即便能定位，掌握个人隐私是否也犯法。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#61 zerovoid</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">哪怕是 gps+基站，也很难定位到具体的楼层，<br/>哪怕是帽子叔叔，也只能蹲在小区门口蹲伏，<br/><br/>他要能通过网络直接定位到你的位置，<br/>那应该和警方联系一下，<br/>把这牛逼的定位技术贡献出来。<br/><br/>当然，如果他发动社会工程学，<br/>那确实是能找得到，不过还得有你的个人信息才行。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#62 zerovoid</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">@<a href=\"/member/willwon1\">willwon1</a> #35 <br/>你手机号都被他知道了，那直接发动社工大法就完事了，<br/>当然社工的本质还是去警察局查个人信息，有手机号不是分分钟的事，<br/>直接报警就完事了，说自己被黑社会威胁了，扫黑除恶办公室来活了。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#63 fend</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">能开户，但具体位置，还是很难的，直接报警。</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#64 c7in7</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">之前看过好像 2k 左右定半天…当然可能是骗子</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#65 Thesara</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">严重程度还不如和外卖骑手起冲突</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#66 florentino</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">大家都在东大生活了这么久了, 为什么还有人质疑啊? 之前新闻不是报道过有临时工通过正式工的账号查询警务系统谋利的嘛  这还是临时工,真有权限的体制内,查你不是分分钟的事情  正确的做法是让他查,真查出来了,再去社交媒体曝光</div></p><hr/>\n<p><strong>#67 JASONWOOD</strong>：<div class=\"reply_content\">等他把你逼到无路可走的时候，就